2 CONT The citizens of Stamford signed an affidavit attesting to the good character of Elizabeth Clauson, on trial for witchcraft. (The original manuscript is owned by The Stamford Historical Society, Inc.)
2 CONT
2 CONT "Our neighbour Stephen Clason having desired us whose names are under written: seeing there is such a report of his wife raised by some among us: that we would speak what we know concerning his said wife and her behaviour among us
2 CONC  for so many year now know all whom it may concern that we do declare that since we have known our said neighbour goodwife Clason we have not known her to be of a contentious frame nor given to use threatening words or to act mali
2 CONC ciously towards her neighbours but hath been civil and orderly towards others in her conversation and not to be a busybody in other men's concerns: given under our hands in Stamford: 4th June 1692:
2 CONT
2 CONT ...Jonas Seely...Samuell Dean, Ann Dean, John Dean, Abigail Dean..."
2 CONT
2 CONT Jonas Seely's will was dated 17 Mar 1702/3 and the inventory was dated 5 Mar 1704/5.
