1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jeanne Majdalany, The Story of the Early Settlers of Stamford, CT 1641 1700, has a map showing George Slawson [Slason] on South Street, next to John Miller, and beyond him, Obadiah Seely. Obadiah was a carpenter w
2 CONC ho built Millers house: after Miller died Obadiah married the widow and raised the Miller boys, presumably moving into the Miller house. 
2 CONT
2 CONT George Slawson had no daughter named Mary that we know of, but his son Thomas did. The records of St Johns Church (per Huntingtons History of Stamford, CT) show that Mary Slason, dau of Thomas and Mary Slason, was baptized Nov 6
2 CONC , 1748. Jonas Seely was born 1653. It is a reasonable assumption that Jonas married this Mary.
2 CONT
