1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Cornelius Seely (
2 CONT  was born 1649-1650 in Stamford, CT, and died Aft. 1714 in Bedford, Westchester Co, NY [age ca65].
2 CONT
2 CONT  He married Priscilla Osborn16 Abt. 1671 in Fairfield, CT,  daughter of Richard Osborn and Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Cornelius Seely and Priscilla Osborn are:
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth Seely, born 1671 in Bedford, Westchester Co, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius Seely, born Abt. 1673 in Bedford, Westchester Co, NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sarah Seely17,18, born Abt. 1676 in Bedford, Westchester Co, NY. She was baptized 17 May 1696, Bedford, Westchester Co, NY
2 CONT
2 CONT  Joseph Seely, born Abt. 1685 in Bedford, Westchester Co, NY; died 1751 in Bedford, Westchester Co, NY. XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius was of Fairfield, CT. He was one of the founders of Bedford, Westchester Co.,  NY where he was an innkeeper. 
2 CONT
2 CONT On 6 Dec, 1687, Cornelius conveyed meadow land to William Clark. About 1688, he was  on a jury in Westchester Co., NY. In 1704, two of the proprietors of the Dibble and  Vineyard Purchase (now part of Westchester Co.) were Corneli
2 CONC us Seeley, Sr. and 
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendants of Obadiah Seeley (SGS #4)--Generations Two through Five  Revised from April 1977 edition 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cornelius Seeley, Jr. At a meeting of parishioners of Christ Church, held 9 Jan 1710,  Cornelius was elected churchwarden. Cornelius deeded land in Bedford, NY to his  children. In 1706/7, he gave land to Sarah and Elizabeth. In 1
2 CONC 709, he gave land to  Joseph. In 1714/5, he gave land to Joseph, Sarah and Cornelius, Jr. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In the Census of 1710, Cornelius and Priscilla appear in Bedford, NY, both age 60. Their  daughter Sarah was living with them, age 34. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children (4) All were born in Bedford, Westchester Co., NY. 
2 CONT
2 CONT XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX
2 CONT
2 CONT Was an Innkeeper in Bedford,NY  where he employed a 17 year old Nehemiah Churcher ( of Westport Ct )
