1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 3. Thomas2 Slawson (Richard1) was born Abt. 1620 in Southwark, Surrey, England  and died Bef. 1655.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated to America with his brother, probably on the ship JONAS in 1637. Was  in Sandwich, MA on Cape Cod in 1638. Moved to Stamford, Fairfield County, CT in  either 1641 or 1642. Apparently he did not like Stamford, and returne
2 CONC d to Plymouth County, MA, where he married, though the name of his wife is unknown. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Child of Thomas Slawson is: 
2 CONT # Josiah3 Slawson, born Abt. 1648 in Sandwich, Barnstable County, Mass.; died Abt. 1683 in Bedford, Westchester County, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Apparently neither George nor Thomas were too well equipped with funds, and being unable to afford passage, they shipped on as sailors. Upon reaching America they went ashore and stayed out of sight until the ship sailed without t
2 CONC hem. This was not an unusual occurrence, as the ships' records show they frequently left America with only a portion of their crews. It would also explain why the names were not on the passenger list.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emigrated to America in 1636, probably arriving on the ship "Jonas". 
2 CONT
2 CONT Authors of local histories pertaining to the New England colonies agree that George and Thomas (2) Slawson were in Lynn, MA in 1637, and that their names were included in the list of those who went from Lynn, Duxbury and Plymouth 
2 CONC to form the new colony at Sandwich. Unfortunately, the early records of Sandwich are very meager, due largely to a fire which destroyed most of them.
2 CONT
2 CONT Links
2 CONT * http://familytreemaker.genealogy.com/users/d/o/n/Darlene-Donovan/GENE1-0002.html#CHILD3
