1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Personal Details
2 CONT Birth: Born approximately 1687 in Stamford, CT.
2 CONT Death: Died around 1749 or 1750 in Bedford, Westchester County, New York, which at the time was roughly 14 miles north of his original home in Greenwich.
2 CONT Parents: He was the eldest son of Stephen Holmes and Mary (Hobby) Holmes. 
2 CONT Marriage and Children
2 CONT Spouse: He married Sarah Seeley on July 29, 1707, in Greenwich, CT.
2 CONT Children: Jonathan and Sarah had at least seven children:
2 CONT Sarah (b. 1708): Married Ebenezer Husted.
2 CONT Martha (b. 1711): Married Jonathan Weeks.
2 CONT Elizabeth (b. 1714).
2 CONT Jonathan Jr. (b. 1716): Married Phebe Haight in 1839.
2 CONT Rachel (b. 1720): Married Nathan Smith Jr.
2 CONT Epenetus (b. 1722): Married Sarah Mead.
2 CONT Susanna (b. 1724). 
2 CONT Life and Land Records
2 CONT Residency: He was a long-time resident of Greenwich, where he was involved in local agriculture and community life.
2 CONT Land Transactions: On March 17, 1727, shortly after his wife Sarah’s death, Jonathan purchased land from his brother, Benjamin Holmes.
2 CONT Relocation: Later in life, he moved to Bedford, NY, likely following family or seeking new agricultural land, where he eventually passed away
