2 CONT * Weaver, Gustine Courson and (Mrs. Clifford Weaver), compiler. The Gustine Compendium. Cincinnati, Ohio: Powell & White, 1929. . Https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/11647/images/dvm_GenMono001186-00004-0?ssrc=&backla
2 CONC bel=Return&pId=4. : Ancestry, 
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/imageviewer/collections/11647/images/dvm_GenMono001186-00113-0?ssrc=&backlabel=Return&pId=201
2 CONT
2 CONT * Owen, Egbert Americua, compiler. Pioneer Sketches of Long Point Settlement:: Or, Norfolk's Foundation Builders and Their Family Genealogies. Toronto, Canada: William Briggs, 1898. Digital. University of Toronto. Internet Archive
2 CONC s. : 2019.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Tasker, Lawrence Hermon, compiler. Papers and Records: The United Empire Loyalist Settlement at Long Point, Lake Erie. Vol II. Toronto: William Briggs, 1900. Digital microfilm. University of Alberta. Archive Org. https://archive
2 CONC .org/details/cihm_28011/page/n7/mode/1up : 2020.
2 CONT
2 CONT *https://archive.org/details/pioneersketcheso00owenuoft/page/46/
2 CONT Abigail Smith, eldest daughter of Father Abraham, married John Gustin, Her children are enumerated in the Gustin genealogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sketch XX The Old Gustin Mill 
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/pioneersketcheso00owenuoft
