1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for NEW YORK with the rank of Private.  [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A133953  DAR Ancestor # A133953]
2 CONT
2 CONT During the war Daniel enlisted under Captain John Sayre, Major John Poppino and Col John Hathorn in 1777 at Ramapo. He served various tours under Capt. Richard Bailey and Col. Heny Wisner. He went as a guard to Easton, PA under Ma
2 CONC j. Poppino. In 1778 he was one of a class that kept guard at Major Decker's fort and Daniel Vannaker's fort.
2 CONT
2 CONT For 40 years Daniel was a deacon in the Florida Presbyterian Church and also served as Trustee. He was also politically active in the community. In 1798 he chaired a meeting in Chester to support Robert R. Livingston as a candidat
2 CONC e for Governor and John Hathorn as Congressman, among others, and was named to a committee of seven to promote their election. He was appointed an assistant justice of Orange County in 1811 and Justice of the Peace in 1814. On Oct
2 CONC ober 3, 1812, a meeting was held in Goshen by the Friends of Peace, Liberty and Commerce--persons opposed to the war. It was made clear that none but those who opposed the war should take part in the proceedings. But when it came 
2 CONC time to nominate a chairman of the meeting, "Dr. Samuel Seward [father of Lincoln's Secretary of State], of Florida, a man whose devoted and passionate attachment to the present administration is well known, rose, and nominated Da
2 CONC niel Poppino, Esq., who is also an avowed partisan of Mr. Madison." Poppino was not, of course, elected.
2 CONT
2 CONT - written by Oliver Popenoe
2 CONT
2 CONT m1 Mary Sayre  Children: - Seth Lord Poppino (-1863) - Eunice Poppino (1785-)
2 CONT
2 CONT m2 Eunice White - Huldah Poppino
