0 @I6000000003061683774@ INDI
1 NAME Joseph /Totten/
2 GIVN Joseph
2 SURN Totten
2 _MARNM Totten
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1721
2 PLAC Hepstead, Long Island, New York
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1800
2 PLAC Goshen, Orange, New York
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ancestor #: A203380
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph TOTTEN 1721-1800
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 1721 and died 1800. Joseph was probably the son of Jasper TOTTEN of
2 CONT
2 CONT Morristown, and probably the same Joseph TOTTEN who was taxed in Warwick,
2 CONT
2 CONT Orange Co., NY in 1775, and whose son John married a Morristown girl in
2 CONT
2 CONT 1793. Joseph Totten probable son of Jasper and grandson of Richard Totten
2 CONT
2 CONT died a resident of Orange Co., NY between April 16, 1800 and May 5, in the
2 CONT
2 CONT same year (Source: The Totten Line) Joseph is mentioned in Jasper's will,
2 CONT
2 CONT probated December 14, 1761 (Source: Wills, New Jersey Archives, Vol. IV,
2 CONT
2 CONT Abstract of Wills) Possibly the same Joseph Totten who owned lots of land
2 CONT
2 CONT in the Adirondack Mountains. His lands were confiscated in 1779-1781.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married ca. 1760 to Mary POPPINO born ca. 1728 at Warwick Township, Orange
2 CONT
2 CONT Co., NY. Mary was a daughter of John Poppino, born ca. 1704 in France and
2 CONT
2 CONT who died in 1785 in New York, and Christian Mary Poppino, also born in
2 CONT
2 CONT France. Mary was a sister of Major John Poppino, a Revolutionary PATRIOT,
2 CONT
2 CONT married to Elizabeth Wood.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Totten, tailor, of Orange County, NY, in his will dated
2 CONT
2 CONT April 16, 1800, probated May 5, 1800, mentioned as heirs, his sons John,
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, Peter, Silas and Levi and his daughter Abigail CURRY ( note: this
2 CONT
2 CONT may be the relationship of the Curry Bros. Mill, with a Totten) Other
2 CONT
2 CONT heirs named without mention of relationship were, Mary MILLER, Christian
2 CONT
2 CONT and Phebe JACKSON and Lydia CLARK. As executioners, he named his sons
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph, Peter, and Silas. No wife is mentioned in the Will. Joseph was
2 CONT
2 CONT listed in the 1790 Census of Warwicktown, Orange Co., NY
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: Last Will of Joseph TOTTEN dated April 16, 1800, probated May 5,
2 CONT
2 CONT 1800, Liber B, Page 158, Surrogate's Court in Goshen, NY
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Ancestor #: A203380
2 CONT
2 CONT  4TH REGT, ORANGE CO MILITIA
