2 DATE 1917
2 ADDR
3 STAE Shackleford
3 CTRY Texas
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Burial record:
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob came to Texas around 1855 and married 
2 CONT
2 CONT (1) Nancy Rama Onstott, born 1842, around 1860. Jacob married 
2 CONT
2 CONT (2) Emeline ‘Emily' Doche (Smith) [West] Seela, the widow of Wilson Jacob West, around 1870-72, probably in Parker County, Texas. Emily was born September 30, 1839 in Texas and died September 2, 1898 in Parker County. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob served in the Confederate Army during the Civil War. He was a private in Company M, First Texas Legion (also known as the Twenty-Seventh Regiment of Texas Cavalry and Whitfield's Legion). He enlisted at Hallettsville, Texas,
2 CONC  on January 1, 1862, and was discharged in 1865. He applied for a pension in December, 1915 while living in Moran, Shackelford County, Texas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob's marker shows a birth date of June 20, 1839 while three census records place his birth in 1834/1835.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----------------------------------------------
