1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   Sylvanus, the son of Dr. John W. Seely was born in PA in 1795 and died in Warren, Trumbull County OH in 1849. He read medicine with his father. In the war of 1812 he entered the service and worked with Dr. Joh b.
2 CONC  Harmon, being present wtih him at the attack of Fort Mackinaw.
2 CONT
2 CONT   Sometime after the War of 1812, he establised his medical practice and lived there the rest of his life.
