1 NAME Oliver /Mabee/
2 GIVN Oliver
2 SURN Mabee
2 _MARNM Mabee
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 10 JAN 1774
2 ADDR
3 CITY Fishkill
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 BURI
2 DATE AFT 2 JUL 1854
2 PLAC Vittoria Baptist Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vittoria
3 STAE Ontario
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 2 JUL 1854
2 PLAC Charlotteville Twnsp
2 ADDR
3 CITY Norfolk County
3 STAE Ontario
3 CTRY Canada
1 OCCU one year as High Constable for District of London,Ont,Canada. sworn inJune 1. 1805
1 TITL Deacon
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Birth==
2 CONT Oliver  Mabee was born on January 10, 1774 in Fishkill, Dutchess County, New York. He was the son of Frederick Mabee and Lavinah (Pelham) Mabee.
2 CONT ==Marriage==
2 CONT Oliver Mabee was married twice.
2 CONT # Oliver Mabee and Mary Decker (Smith) Mabee married on June 7, 1795 in Turkey Point, Norfolk , Upper Canada, British America.
2 CONT # Oliver Mabee and Rachel (Smith) Shearer, widowed sister of Mary Decker (Smith) Mabee married on May 4, 1844. 
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT Oliver Mabee and Mary Decker (Smith) Mabee
2 CONT # Lydia Elizabeth Mabee 
2 CONT # Peter Mabee
2 CONT # Miriam Mabee
2 CONT # Gabriel Mabee
2 CONT # Naomi Mabee
2 CONT # Rachel Mabee
2 CONT # Julia Mabee
2 CONT # Rhoda Mabee
2 CONT # Abigail Mabee
2 CONT # Oliver Mabee
2 CONT ==Death and Burial==
2 CONT Oliver Mabee passed away on July 2, 1854 Charlotteville Township, Norfolk County, Ontario, Canada, at age 80. He was buried in Vittoria Baptist Cemetery, Vittoria, Norfolk County, Ontario, Canada.
2 CONT ==Biographical Information==
2 CONT One of the pioneer deacons
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpt from Pioneer Sketches of Long Point Settlement, E.A.Owen, Sketch LXII.
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/pioneersketcheso00owenuoft/page/316/
2 CONT
2 CONT "Oliver was a mere lad during his experience on Turkey Point, being about sixteen years old at the time of Governor Simcoe's visit.  His mother was awarded a U.E. Loyalist land grant of six hundred acres on the lake front as the w
2 CONC ife of a U.E. Loyalist.  Oliver's land was located near Vittoria, but he sold it and bought Jesse Smith's grant, being Lot 17, in the 5th concession. Here he settled and reared his family.  He married Mary, daughter of the origina
2 CONC l Abraham Smith.  
2 CONT
2 CONT  Mr Mabee was a God-fearing man...For years he and Joseph Kitchen led the singing, alternately, in the old Vittoria Baptist church and many of the old people remember with pleasure the whole-hearted earnestness that characterized 
2 CONC his style of singing.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Mabee was noted for his loyality to country..... He served one year as High Constable for the District of London, being sworn into office, June 1st, 1805.  In the war of 1812 he was captain of a company of militia and took 
2 CONC part in the battle of Lundy's Lane.  
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/135315197/oliver-mabee: accessed 10 November 2023), memorial page for Oliver Mabee Sr. (11 Aug 1773–2 Jul 1854), Find a Grave Memorial ID 135315197, citing V
2 CONC ittoria Baptist Cemetery, Vittoria, Norfolk County, Ontario, Canada; Maintained by Joseph R. Klett (contributor 47554493).
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=135315197 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jun 12 2017, 18:08:13 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Mabee (1773-1854)Charlotteville Township, Norfolk County, Ontario, Canada, at age 80
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Mabee (1773-1854 and Mary Smith (1775-1844)	
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver Mabee, the son of Frederick Mabee and Levinah Pelham (?-1823) was born in Dutchess County, New York on 10 Aug 1773.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver's father remained loyal to the Crown during the American Revolution. In 1781, Frederick brought his family to British occupied New York City. In 1783 when the British evacuated New York City, Frederick and his family sailed
2 CONC  as part of the "October Fleet" on the Sally to the Saint John River Valley in what is now New Brunswick.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick settled first in the town of Carleton but later moved to Queensbury, York County on the Saint John River west of Fredericton. Not satisfied with the quality of the land, Frederick sold his property and moved his family t
2 CONC o Upper Canada in 1792.
2 CONT
2 CONT Frederick arrived at Long Point Bay in the spring of 1793, having overwintered at Quebec, and began to clear land on Turkey Point. Regrettably, he died the following year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Oliver, who was nineteen when he arrived at the Long Point Settlement, married Mary Smith (1775-1844), another daughter of Abraham Smith. In Oliver's 1797 Upper Canada Land Petition he stated that he had received 200 acres of land
2 CONC , but was requesting an additional grant. The request was denied. During the War of 1812 he rose to the rank of Captain in the 1st Regiment, Norfolk Militia. After Mary’s death in 1844, Oliver married Rachel Shearer, the widow of 
2 CONC Robert Shearer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mabee, Dr. Oliver R., “The Ancestry and Hardships of Frederick Mabee,” Ontario Historical Society, Papers and Records, 1927, Vol. 24, p.439-442,
2 CONT
2 CONT Source: http://stalkingdeadpeople.blogspot.com/2017/01/the-baptist-pioneers-of-vittoria.html
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Norfolk County,West Ontario. Canada
