1 NOTE {geni:about_me} John Gustin - https://sites.google.com/site/longpointsettlers/pioneer-sketches/owen-chapter-20
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gustin was the son of Eliphalet Gustin and Freelove Wightman of Sussex County, New Jersey. He married first to Abigail Smith by about 1783. They arrived, with their first two daughters, in the Niagara Penninsula, Upper Canada
2 CONC  (Ontario) in 1787, having reportedly spent several years in New York State looking for his parents. They first settled on a 160-acre grant on Four Mile Creek and Lake Erie in Bertie Twp., Welland Co.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1794, John petitioned for land at the Long Point Settlement in Norfolk Co. He moved to that location in 1796, and in 1798 exchanged his land in Bertie Twp. for 300 acres in Charlotteville Twp., Norfolk Co. (Long Point Settlemen
2 CONC t). He established his log cabin on Lot 22 on Young's Creek.- https://sites.google.com/site/longpointsettlers/upper-canada-land-petitions/petitions-g
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gustin in record of Abraham Smith - 
2 CONT Land Records: Charlotteville
2 CONT Date: 20 March 1797
2 CONT Page: 620
2 CONT Official: Thomas Welch, Extra Dept Surveror 
2 CONT Petitioner: Abraham Smith
2 CONT Improvements: Abraham Smith - 
2 CONT Currently: Lot 13, 14, 15 of 4th Concession and Lots 13, 14, 15 of 8th Concession
2 CONT Petitions for: 
2 CONT Lot No 14, 15 of 5th Concession, L 20, 7th Concession. L(to) 1 of 10th Concession for Mill Seat
2 CONT
2 CONT for John Gustin, Husband to Abagail Daughter of "Abm. Smith - Lot No. 20, L 22 of 3rd Concession Lot 19 - 4th concession, one of those Lots claimed by a Remlt of Council & Warrant, the other two by Minister of Council
2 CONT
2 CONT For Oliver Mabee, Husband of Mary Daughter of said Abraham Lot 21 - 4th concession, Lot 10 5th Concession
2 CONT
2 CONT For Son Samuel Smith No 22 - 5th Concession; L 10? - 7th Concession
2 CONT
2 CONT For Son Jesse Smith - 17 - 5th Concession; L 2 - 10th Concession
2 CONT
2 CONT For Son William Smith - 10? 6th Concession, 19 of 6th concession
2 CONT
2 CONT For Son Isaac Smith - 21 - 6th concession; 16 - 6th concession
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac Smith has improved on No 15 - 5th concession; 15, 16 - 6th concession 
2 CONT
2 CONT Note: Olver Mabee has Improved & lives on Lot No. 21 by TW Dt
2 CONT
2 CONT Signed: Thomas Welch, Extra Dept Surveyor
2 CONT ----------
2 CONT
2 CONT John was a farmer, grist miller, and sawmiller. - https://archive.org/details/ancestryofherber02gust/page/1188/
2 CONT
2 CONT He was listed as a private in the Charlotteville Militia in 1798 & 1799. He served on the grand jury of the London District Court of Quarter Sessions from 1800 to 1809. He was also appointed a constable in 1801.
2 CONT
2 CONT About 1804, John was a founding member of the Baptist Church at Vittoria. He built a mill on his homestead about 1805-10, and reportedly operated mills at more than one location. In 1808, he was bequeathed $100 in the will of his 
2 CONC uncle, Benajah Gustin of Sussex Co., NJ. - https://babel.hathitrust.org/cgi/pt?id=aeu.ark:/13960/t4jm3z107&seq=10
2 CONT
2 CONT He married second to Elizabeth Rogers on 20 July 1814 in Norfolk, Upper Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gustin witnessed the deed dated September 21, 1814 for Lot 17 7th Concession - Grantor: Abraham Smih by Hannah Smith (daughter) divisee and the Grantee: Simon Mabee 
2 CONT "Norfolk, Ontario, Canada records," images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSLG-K3Q3-V?view=explore : Feb 11, 2026), image 649 of 741; .
2 CONT Image Group Number: 008198249
2 CONT
2 CONT On April 16, 1816, John Gustin of Charlotteville, Norfolk County, Upper Canada, sold a parcel of 120 acres (part of lot number 20, third concession) to James Smith for £300, witnessed by Francis L. Walsh and Elsey Walsh. A memoria
2 CONC l of this transaction was registered, referencing deeds and witnesses, and officially recorded on July 2, 1819. The boundaries of the land, as well as neighboring owners Platt Wood and Robert, are described in detail. The deed ens
2 CONC ures ownership for James Smith and his heirs forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT Location: Bk 4 Memorial 1041 
2 CONT
2 CONT "Norfolk, Ontario, Canada records," images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSLG-L7QN-K?view=explore : Feb 11, 2026), image 264 of 650; .
2 CONT Image Group Number: 008198250
2 CONT
2 CONT On February 5, 1821, James Mitchell received a property transfer in York, witnessed by several individuals and later officially registered in May 1821. An indenture dated April 26, 1821, documents the sale of land in Charlottevill
2 CONC e, Upper Canada, from John Gustin and his wife Elizabeth to Matthew H. Tisdale for sixty-two pounds and ten shillings. The property comprised part of lot 22 in the township’s third concession. Key individuals involved include Eliz
2 CONC abeth Gustin, wife and co-granter, and others who witnessed and registered the transactions.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Norfolk, Ontario, Canada records," images, FamilySearch (https://www.familysearch.org/ark:/61903/3:1:3Q9M-CSLG-L7QD-S?view=explore : Feb 11, 2026), image 379 of 650; .
2 CONT Image Group Number: 008198250
2 CONT
2 CONT He died between April and September  1821, presumably at his homestead in Charlotteville, Norfolk, Upper Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Gustin's Will  30 October 1821 at Charlotteville Township, Norfolk County, Ontario, Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT  "Will of John Gustin, Farmer, mentions wife, Abigail, sons Charles and Eliphalet Gustin, 
2 CONT daughters, Sophia, Jemima, Rachel, Katy and Freelove Gustin, and daughter, Abigail Mabee."
2 CONT
2 CONT Executors were Sophia Gustin, Samuel Smith, and Peter Teeple 
2 CONT
2 CONT Additional details - The will was not dated (apparently made out around September 1800)
2 CONT
2 CONT Petitioners: Elizabeth Gustin, widow of John Gustin; Peter Teeple; Samuel Smith - petition not dated
2 CONT
2 CONT Affidavit by Sophia Gustin Wood, dated September 26, 1821 stated that John Gustin did not name all his children in the will. 
2 CONT Charles Gustin did not remember witnessing the will.
2 CONT
2 CONT Inventory of estate completed October 22, 1821 by James Smith and Jacob Potts Junior."2 
2 CONT * London District, Upper Canada (Ontario, Canada). Surrogate Court. Estate Files 1800 - 1839
2 CONT Estate No: 89 Name: John Gustin Date of Death: c. 1821
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.ancestry.com/mediaui-viewer/collection/1030/tree/62264607/person/432021192520/media/5988043d-b129-4110-9a97-7893c3ac0eae?galleryindex=6&sort=-created
2 CONT ==Note==
2 CONT The creator of this memorial, Tom Hoot, placed John's and his wife's memorials in the Ingersoll Rural Cemetery with eldest daughters Abigail Mabee and Sophia Wood. I am not ware of any documentation of John's grave. It seems more 
2 CONC likely, based on the information I have, that John and his first wife were buried in the Vittoria Baptist Cemetery given that they were founding members of the church. Her parents and their eldest son Charles are interred there. I
2 CONC f this is the case, then no gravestone survive for them. Any information to help resolve this question will be much appreciated. --Joseph R. Klett Note: See above relative to the burial location.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=45401946 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 26 2017, 18:19:21 UTC''
2 CONT ==Sources==
