1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Birth==
2 CONT Abigail (Gustin) Mabee was born about 1783, probably in Sussex County, New Jersey. She was the eldest child of John Gustin, Sr. and Abigail (Smith) Gustin. 
2 CONT ==Marriage==
2 CONT Simon Mabee and Abigail (Gustin) Mabee married around 1799. 
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT Abigail and Simon had 12 children together, as follows:
2 CONT # Elizabeth, born Jan. 1800--linked below;
2 CONT # Anna, born abt. 1802--linked below;
2 CONT # Samuel H., born abt. 1804, married Hannah, died 24 Apr. 1872 in Altemount, IL;
2 CONT # Walter Bishop, born 9 Nov. 1805--linked below;
2 CONT # Nancy, born abt. 1808--linked below;
2 CONT # Susanna Sophia, born 28 Aug. 1809--linked below;
2 CONT # John G., died in childhood;
2 CONT # Rachel Cary, born 1813--linked below;
2 CONT # Lovina (twin), born 10 Nov. 1815--linked below;
2 CONT # Abigail (twin), born 10 Nov. 1815, married Charles Harris in 1833, died in Sep. 1901 in Windsor, Ontario;
2 CONT # Oliver Dennis, born 31 Aug. 1817--linked below;
2 CONT # Mary, died in childhood. 
2 CONT ==Death==
2 CONT Abigail (Gustin) Mabee passed away on June 17, 1871 in West Oxford Township, Oxford County, Ontario, Canada. She was buried in Ingersoll Rural Cemetery, Ingersoll, Oxford County Municipality, Ontario, Canada. 
2 CONT ==Supporting Information==
2 CONT # "Abigail Gustin, eldest daughter of John, married Simon Mabee, the old pioneer Baptist preacher, and settled in Oxford."pg 126.  https://archive.org/details/pioneersketcheso00owenuoft/page/126/
2 CONT # "Simon Mabee, second son of Frederick, was born in 1778, and was about fifteen years old when the family settled on Turkey Point. In 1799, he married Abigail', daughter of John Gustin, and, for a time, owned the land upon which 
2 CONC the larger and better portion of the old village of Vittoria is built." page 41 https://archive.org/details/pioneersketcheso00owenuoft/page/41/
2 CONT
2 CONT * Pioneer Sketches of Long Point Settlement: Or, Norfolk's Foundation Builders ...By Egbert Americus Owen
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Acknowledgement==
2 CONT Note: Heartfelt thanks to Tom Hoot for creating this memorial and to Steven Shinbin for the gravestone image.
