1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Ebenezer Seeley Bartlett'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9421427/ebenezer_seeley_bartlett
2 CONT
2 CONT A native of Newburg, Orange County, New York. D.A.R. records show he enlisted Dec. 1775 (aged 16 years & 2 months) and served with the New York Militia. He was in the battles of Harlem, White Plains and Fort Montgomery; he served 
2 CONC until 1781.  In 1838 he came to Illinois with his sons, settling in Clark County, and died in December the same year.  He lies buried in the York Cemetery and his grave has been marked by the Walter Burdick Chapter, D.A.R., of Mar
2 CONC shall.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebenezer Bartlett was initiated October 16, 1793 into Union Lodge No. 30 F.&A.M. (Free and Accepted Masons), Newtown (now Elmira), New York.
2 CONT Contributor: J. Kelsey Jones (47370830) •* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/9421427/ebenezer-seeley-bartlett Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2024, 10:44:2
2 CONC 0 UTC''
2 CONT
