1 NOTE http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~ilclark/bartlett.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Excerpts from letters written to Lulu Reed Boss by John Bartlett b. 1853, d. 1936 who lived at Salt Lick, Ky. for a time. He was a great grandson of Pioneer William Bartlett. These letters were dated 21 Feb. 1936, 26 Feb. 1936 and
2 CONC  7 March 1936:
2 CONT "My father called William Bartlett granddad. My grandfather's name was Samuel Bartlett. Samuel had a brother EBENEZER. My dad always told me that William Bartlett owned Blue Licks and several thousand acres of land around Blue Lic
2 CONC ks, including the place he is buried, which is about three miles from the Licks on what is now called the Hammond farm. I have been to the grave of William Bartlett many times ...... on his tombstone is this simple inscription "Wi
2 CONC lliam Bartlett, Pioneer, died 1820".
2 CONT
2 CONT Will of Ebeneezer Bartlett
2 CONT Dated October 30, 1843, Carthage, Hancock Co, IL
2 CONT Will Records, Hancock Co, IL, Will Book G, pages 6-8
2 CONT “I Ebenezer BARTLETT of the county of Hancock and State of Illinois being of sound mind do make this my last will and testament in manner and form following:
2 CONT First it is my Will that my funeral expenses, and all debts be fully paid.
2 CONT Secondly I give to my wife, Rebecca, all the remainder of my property, real and personal during her lifetime or widowhood with full power while she remain my widow until death to dispose of it as she think proper but if she shall 
2 CONC marry or die without first making a will then it is my will that my daughters Malinda DUNCAN, Sally Ann CRANDER (or Crowder) and Mary Jane BARTLETT have fifty dollars each then the balance of my property be equally divided between
2 CONC  my two sons viz: Franklin J. BARTLETT, Henry J. BARTLETT, and my three daughters Malinda DUNCAN, Sally Ann CROWDER and Mary Jane BARTLETT, and Lastly I name my son Franklin J. BARTLETT and William DARNALL executors.
2 CONT In Testimony whereof I set my hand and seal this 30th day of October A.D. 1843. 
2 CONT (Signed) Ebenezer BARTLETT 
2 CONT Witnesses: William DARNALL, Nathan H. GRAFTON"
2 CONT Will of Ebenezer Seeley Bartlett was proven Dec. 1843.
2 CONT A note from Mrs. Alice Evarts Hurd, widow of Samuel W. Widney of Denver, Colo. "Ebenezer Bartlett and wife Rebecca Standiford left Nicholas Co. Ky. ca. 1828-30 and went to Springfield, IL, where they lived four years, and then to 
2 CONC Pike Co. IL, where they stayed two years and finally to Hancock Co. IL, where he owned a grist and saw mill and died there”. -LMHW.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1818, an Ebeneezer Bartlett, of Salem, Massachusetts, received a warrant on land in McDonough county, in the Miltary Land Bounty section of west Illinois: SE S19, 4N, 2W, N. 4th PM (160 acres), for his service in the War of 181
2 CONC 2, 9th Infantry, US Army (Capt. Turner Crooker’s Company), in the Battle of Chippewa; he sold it immediately in Washington DC. This land is on Grindstone Creek, a tributary to the LaMoine River, south of Macomb. I don't know if th
2 CONC is was the same Ebeneezer.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ebeneezer (D-1) is in the taxes of Nicholas co, from their beginning in 1800 until 1826; he is in the 1830 Census of Fleming co KY, p16, signed off 27 November.
2 CONT On 25 October 1830, Eb bought Lot #4, Block 31, in the town of Springfield (7th and Madison), Sangamon county, Illinois, which he sold on 3 Aug. 1833. On May 16, 1831 Eb homesteaded 80 acres in the southern part of town, the S½, N
2 CONC E¼, S6, T15N, R5W; he sold this to John Crowder, brother of his son-in-law Albert Crowder, Oct. 14, 1834. 
2 CONT Eb's son Frank was married to Lydia Karges in Pike county to the west on 6 Jan.1834. On March 12, 1834, Aquilla Hildreth, Eb's son-in-law by his daughter Elizabeth, received his patent on the NW¼ of S32, T3S, R2W, which he sold to
2 CONC  Frank Bartlett in May 1834; 1835 is the earliest date Aquilla had a child born in Illinois. In 1836, Eb sold the NW¼ of the NE¼, T3S, R2W, next door; in 1840 he received another patent on the same land, and his son Henry J. recei
2 CONC ved one for the ¼¼ to the east. Eb is listed there in the 1840 Census with his son Frank J. This land is just south of Chambersburg. 
2 CONT In September 1837, his son Henry J. was married in Hancock co to the north, his daughter Malinda was married there in 1838; Aquilla Hildreth received a patent on land in Section 1, R5W, T5N in 1840. At the same time, Eb and Frank 
2 CONC received patents there, in Hancock township, about 4 miles northwest of the town of Colmar. Frank’s deed says he was in Pike county at the time. This land is on the Lemoine river, next to a grist mill then owned by Samuel Brown. F
2 CONC rank was owner of a mill, on Crooked Creek, where he sawed wood and ground wheat. His neighbors in the 1840 Census are the same ones listed as local homesteaders; these people were the pioneers in the area. Eb died 2 Dec. 1843, an
2 CONC d is most likely buried either in the Bloyd/Belknap, or the Brown cemeteries, which have many unmarked graves.
2 CONT
2 CONT Census Data for Ebeneezer Seeley Bartlett
2 CONT Statistical analysis of Census records indicates 7 girls and 2 boys.
2 CONT The identities of the two older males in the 1810 are unknown.
2 CONT Nicholas Co Fleming Co Fleming Co Hancock Co.
2 CONT 1810 1820 1830 1840
2 CONT 2 males 16-26 2 males under 10 1 male 10-15 1 male 60-70
2 CONT 1 male 26-45 2 males 10-16 1 male 15-20 1 female 10-15
2 CONT 4 females under 10 1 male 26-45 1 male 50-60 1 female 15-20
2 CONT 1 female 26-45 1 female under 10 1 female under 5 1 female 50-60
2 CONT 3 females 10-16 1 female 5-10
2 CONT 1 female 16-26 1 female 10-15
2 CONT 1 female 26-45 1 female 50-60
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Ebeneezer Seeley Bartlett and Rebecca Standiford, all born in Kentucky:
2 CONT E-1 Sarah Bartlett (5) m. Lapham.
2 CONT E-2 Elizabeth Bartlett (5) b. 1805, m. 14 Mar. 1822 KY, Aquilla Hildreth.
2 CONT E-3 Lucinda Bartlett (5) b. 30 Nov. 1807, m. 11 May 1824, Mason co KY, Robert Fristoe.
2 CONT E-4 Eliza Bartlett (5) b. abt. 1808, m. 1 Oct. 1826, Nicholas co KY, Josiah McCabe.
2 CONT E-5 Franklin James Bartlett (5) b. 1810-1813, d. abt. 1843, m. 1 July 1834, Pike co. IL, Lydia Karges.
2 CONT E-6 Henry Jackson Bartlett (5) b. 7 March 1818, m. 7 Sept. 1837, Hancock co. IL, Isabella Huddleston.
2 CONT E-7 Mary Jane Bartlett (5) b. 1819 KY, m. 9 May 1844, Hancock co IL, James Legrande Sanford.
2 CONT E-8 Malinda Bartlett (5) b.12 Nov. 1820, d. Nov. 1903; m. 13 Dec.1838, Hancock co. IL, Wm. Preston Duncan.
2 CONT E-9 Sally Ann Bartlett (5) b. ca.1822, d.1848, Sangamon IL; m. 29 Dec. 1840, Hancock IL, Albert G. Crowder.
