0 @I6000000027592187164@ INDI
1 NAME Samuel C. /Holmes/
2 GIVN Samuel C.
2 SURN Holmes
2 _MARNM Holmes
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 25 MAR 1760
1 DEAT
2 DATE 19 MAR 1813
2 ADDR
3 CITY Cambridge
3 STAE VT
3 CTRY United States
1 TITL Rev.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Revolutionary War Veteran'''
2 CONT
2 CONT From Fold3 documents/ Statement of Salina (Sallina) Holmes, widow of Samuel Holmes:
2 CONT
2 CONT Prior to 1780, served as a Private in the New York troops under Col. Van Vichlan (? unsure of name-D.G.)for at least 1 year or more. He then served one year or more in Capt. Allen's and Capt.Safford's Company at different times fr
2 CONC om 1780 to the close of the Revolutionary War.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Holmes, Samuel, Sallena or Salina, W18066, BLW (Bounty Land Warrant)#31279-160-55 NY &VT line, sol enlisted at Stillwater, N.Y., and later moved to Bennington, VT., and also enlisted there, and he married there to Salina or Sallen
2 CONC a, daughter of Capt. Scott and his wife (not named), who was a sister of Capt. Joseph Safford, and they were married 11 Sept., 1782; sol. died 19 March, 1813 at Cambridge in Lamoille Co., VT. and widow applied there 18 Sept., 1844
2 CONC , aged 77; children were: Salina, b 12 Jan., 1784, at Bennington, VT; Abigail b. 18 Jan. 1786 at Poundwell, VT.; Anna b. 23 Dec., 1787 at Bennington, VT.; Theron b. 14 Mar .1790,; Levi b. 15 Feb. 1792; William, or Billy, b. 8 May,
2 CONC  1796, the last three children were born at Cambridge, VT., Emela, John, Samuel, who died as an infant. Samuel 2nd was born after sol. had died; a daughter, (not named), was the wife of Augustus Young, a member of Congress from VT
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Elder Samuel married Salina Scott in Bennington, VT, Nov. 9, 1782 [source is a rare genealogy by Sarah Robinson, "Historical Genealogy of the Robinson, Safford, etc. Families" (1837).]The Robinson genealogy states that Salina marr
2 CONC ied Elder Samuel "son of Sam'l Holmes, of Bennington."The Robinson entry proves that Elder Samuel's father's name is Samuel and they were both lived in Bennington, VT, on Nov. 9, 1782.
2 CONT
2 CONT These historical records document that a John and John Jr. Holmes, a Samuel Holmes and my ancestor, Elder Samuel Holmes, lived near Bennington VT at times between 1765 and 1782.I have not been able to document the conjectural rela
2 CONC tionship between Samuel and Elder Samuel; perhaps you can help prove or disprove the link.
2 CONT
2 CONT I think it is probably not a coincidence that Samuel’s younger brother, Lemuel, moved to Newbury VT sometime after his marriage to Abigail Bicknell in 1761.We can theoretically place five Holmes men in VT during the same time peri
2 CONC ods, who were probably blood relatives, and who probably all moved from Ashford CT to make their living as pioneers in the wilderness.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have fairly complete records for Elder Samuel’s descendants.Elder Samuel fought in the Battle of Bennington in 1777.Salina Scott’s ancestors are interesting.One Eulailia Marche Burt was laid out for dead in England and put in he
2 CONC r coffin, but signs of life appearing at her funeral she recovered, came to New England and was mother of 19 children.
2 CONT
2 CONT Who are John and Keziah Holmes? John Jr.’s wife’s name is Lois Tiffany.What was Samuel’s second wife’s name, if he had one, and what are the daughters’ names from his first marriage to Mary Evans?
2 CONT
