1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jacob was the son of Israel Wood Sr. and Ruth Gould, who were Loyalists during the American Revolutionary War. In 1783, while an infant, he was evacuated from Long Island, New York, with his parents and siblings ab
2 CONC oard the John and Jane. He was baptized by Anglican minister Rev. Richard Clarke at Kingston, Kings Co., NB, 3 July 1786.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jacob moved with his family to the Long Point Settlement in Upper Canada (Ontario), settling at Woodhouse Township, Norfolk Co., 1799. He married Sophia Gustin on 16 May 1804.
2 CONT
2 CONT He purchased 44 acres in Lot 14, Concession 1, West Oxford Twp., Oxford Co., from Oliver Rouse, making this his homestead. He later added 30 acres in the lot purchased from Comfort Sage.
2 CONT
2 CONT He was a constable in Charlotteville, Norfolk Co., in 1806, and served as a private in Robinson's Company of Militia in 1814, during the war with the United States. He was living in Oxford Twp. in 1823 when his wife signed off on 
2 CONC the remainder of her father's lands.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in West Oxford Twp. Note: Heartfelt thanks to Tom Hoot for creating this memorial.
