1 NAME James /Wood/
2 GIVN James
2 SURN Wood
2 _MARNM Wood
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC Burgessville Baptist Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Burgessville
3 STAE Ontario
3 CTRY Canada
1 BIRT
2 DATE 11 JUL 1791
2 ADDR
3 CITY Waterborough
3 STAE New Brunswick
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 12 OCT 1865
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} James was the son of Israel Wood and Ruth Gould. He was baptized by Anglican minister Rev. Richard Clarke at Waterborough, Queens Co., NB, 26 Dec. 1792. In 1799, he moved with his family to the Long Point Settlemen
2 CONC t in Upper Canada (Ontario), settling in Woodhouse Twp., Norfolk Co. He might be the same James Wood who received a grant on Lot 22, 5th concession of Walsingham, 1807.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Catharine Gustin on 19 Jan. 1817. They were living in Oxford Twp., Oxford Co., ON, in 1823, when his wife signed off on the remainder of her father's lands. He purchased Lot 8, 8th Concession, East Oxford Twp., Oxford C
2 CONC o., 28 April 1823, which he made his homestead. He sold 85 acres of this farm to his son Isaiah in 1844.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his wife were members of the New Connexion Methodist faith. They had 7 children, as follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. James Harmon (b. 1818) m. Mary S. Underwood; 2. Sydney Gustin (b. 1819) m. Harriet; 3. Isaiah (b. 1821) m. Lavina Chapman Woodrow; 4. Alanson Gustin (1822-1861) m. Azoletta Fairchild; 5. Ruth Philena (b. 1826) m. William G. Har
2 CONC kness; 6. Rebecca Ann (b. 1829) m. Thomas Grey; and 7. Elgin Wood (abt. 1838 - aft. 1852). Note: Heartfelt thanks to Tom Hoot for creating this memorial and steven shinbin for the gravestone image.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=45418547 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 29 2017, 19:12:01 UTC''
2 CONT
