1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Isaiah Wood was born March 20, 1821, and Sept. 14, 1841 he married Lavina Chapman Woodrow, daughter of the late Joseph Woodrow, of Norwich and they located for a time in Michigan, later moving to Iowa. On May 24, 1
2 CONC 861, they returned to Ontario, and located at Sarnia, operating a farm on the London road. There Mr. Wood died in 1899, and there his wife still resides at the age of eighty-five. Politically he was a Reformer. Both he and wife we
2 CONC re members of the Methodist Church. They had these children born to them: Sidney G., a resident of Detroit; Joseph, a farmer of Sarnia township; Lanson H., a resident of North Dakota; Elgin, of Sarnia; James F., deceased, who was 
2 CONC with his brother Elgin, in the fruit business; Nancy, wife of Uriah Varnum, of Sarnia township; W.O. deceased; Mrs. Johnston of Minnesota; Mrs, Woodhall of Minnesota; and Franklin, deceased.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://archive.org/details/recordlambton00beeruoft/page/n4/mode/2up Commemorative biographical record of the county of Lambton, Ontario... : containing biographical sketches of prominent and representative citizens 
2 CONC and many of the early settled families] (1906)
2 CONT
2 CONT husband of lavina c woodrus. father of lovetha (george d johnston), ninie, annie c, wm elgin, joseph s (jane calvert), alanson h (alice dewar)
