2 CONT ==Birth==
2 CONT Salome F. Stone was born on April 25, 1837 in Vermillion, Erie County, Ohio. She was the daughter of John Stone and |Freelove (Gustin) Manuel Stone. Her father may have been https://www.geni.com/people/John-Stone-III/5678040426580
2 CONC 060202 
2 CONT ==Marriage==
2 CONT Nelson Little and Salome (Stone) Little married around 1859.
2 CONT ==Child==
2 CONT Capt. John Warren Little was their adopted son.
2 CONT ==Property==
2 CONT St. Clair Mortgages - Saloma F Little to Eliphalet G. Manuel on 18 July 1870
2 CONT Dated: 26 June 1870  
2 CONT $ 1000
2 CONT being land formerly owned by F. D. Manuel and conveyed to him to Freelove Stone and by said F. Stone to Salomia F. Little 
2 CONT Executed by Saloma F Little & Nelson Little
2 CONT ==Death==
2 CONT Salome (Stone) Little passed away on March 9, 1900 at South Military Street, Port Huron, St. Clair County, Michigan at the age of 62 years,  10 months, and 12 days of a pulmonary embolism. She was buried in site K 035 in Lakeside 
2 CONC Cemetery, Port Huron, St. Clair County, Michigan.
2 CONT
