1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Caroline Sturges, a pioneer resident this county, died at the family residence, on the river road this morning, aged 69 years. Mrs. Sturges had lived in the house in which she died since 1847. She was a well a
2 CONC nd favorably known and was a member of the Congregational church of this city. The deceased was a sister of E. G. Manuel and the mother of Mrs. Geo. W. Howe. The funeral services will probably be held from the residence on Thursda
2 CONC y of this week. 
2 CONT 30 March 1886
