1 NOTE {geni:about_me} E. G. MANUEL lives on Section 21, township of Port Huron, was born at Long Point, Can., February 13, 1821. At five years of age he went to Cleveland, Ohio, and remained in Northern Ohio until August, 1842, at which
2 CONC  time he went to Northern Indiana and commenced business in Valparaiso, in 1843, and was married at La Porte, March 4, 1847, to Miss Sarah Alsop, a native of England; remained in Northern Indiana until December, 1858, but his heal
2 CONC th having become impaired, hoping for good results, he came to Michigan, and settled on a farm near Mount Clemens, Macomb County, where he stayed two years, and in May, 1861, moved to this county, and settled on the St. Clair Rive
2 CONC r, and since then has resided here without engaging in any particular business. Commenced life poor, and if he has met with success, it is the result of the combined efforts of himself and wife. Although something of a worker in h
2 CONC is party, has never become an office-holder to any extent; has, however, held the office of Highway Commissioner several times, also Town Clerk, Justice of the Peace, etc., and has served as School Director in School District No. 
2 CONC 3, for seventeen consecutive years; owns 170 acres of land adjoining the city limits of Port Huron. They have but one child, Fred W.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sara Melissa Alsop Manuel
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/michiganhistoric21michuoft/page/248/mode/1up
