3 CITY Kilworth
3 STAE Ontario
3 CTRY Canada
1 DEAT
2 DATE 23 JAN 1920
2 ADDR
3 CITY Saint Thomas
3 STAE Ontario
3 CTRY Canada
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Occupation - Physician and surgeon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eliphalet was born at Kilworth, Middlesex, Ontario Son of - Eliphalet GUSTIN and Mary Ann EDWARDS.
2 CONT
2 CONT Eliphalet and Eliza married on 23 September 1890 at St. Thomas, Elgin, Ontario.
2 CONT
2 CONT S= "London Township Pioneers", by Frederick T. Rosser, Mika Publishing, Belleville, Ontario, CANADA; ISBN0-919302-95-5; p. 133
2 CONT    Eliphalet Wilbur was born at Kilworth May 7, 1834.  He graduated from the London Grammar School and from Trinity College, University of Toronto, and Rolph's School of Medicine.  While an undergraduate he studied in the office o
2 CONC f Dr. C. B. Hall in St.  Thomas.  He was only twenty years old when he graduated and since the law required all doctors to be over the age of twenty-one, he secured a permit to practise for one year.  He began in partnership with 
2 CONC Dr. Travers of Fingal.  The next year he took his medical diploma from Cobourg College Department of Medicine. He practised in Fingal for ten years. At first he visited his patients on horseback.  It was said at the time that Dr. 
2 CONC Gustin rode farther on horseback than any other man in the London district in one year's time.  He went to St. Thomas in the 1860's and practised medicine there until his death in 1920.  He became surgeon for the Great Western Rai
2 CONC lway, and continued when it became the Grand Trunk, and also for the Wabash and the Canadian Pacific.  He was coroner for the county of Elgin for about fifty years.  In 1872, after much persuasion, he stood as Conservative candida
2 CONC te in the federal election and cut the majority of his Liberal opponent, George E. Casey, to a few hundred votes.  For this he received the personal congratulations of Sir John A. Macdonald.  He held many public offices, among whi
2 CONC ch were mayor of St. Thomas in 1883, master in the Masonic Lodge, surgeon for the 25th Elgin Infantry, and president of the South Western Farmers' and Mechanics' Saving and Loan Co. His first wife was Dr. Traver's widow.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=41763303 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 29 2017, 20:46:49 UTC''
