2 CONT Co A 184th Inf 
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 184th New York Infantry Regiment
2 CONT
2 CONT The 184th New York Infantry lost 1 officer and 10 enlisted men killed or mortally wounded and 27 enlisted men to disease during the Civil War.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1864 Organized at Oswego, N.Y. under Colonel Wardwell G. Robinson, Lt. Colonel William P. McKinley and Major William D. Ferguson for one year’s service
2 CONT
2 CONT September 12	Companies A, B, D and F Mustered in at Elmira, N.Y. and left State for the Shenandoah Valley under Major W. D. Ferguson. Attached to 1st Brigade, 3rd Division, 6th Army Corps.
2 CONT
2 CONT September 16	Companies C, E, G, H, I and K left State for Bermuda Hundred, Va., Dept. of Virginia and North Carolina under Colonel Robinson.
2 CONT
2 CONT October 19	 Battle of Cedar Creek
2 CONT
2 CONT Companies A, B, D and F were engaged under Major Ferguson, losing killed or mortally wounded First Lieutenant Augustus Phillips of Company D; Corporal John M. Wing and Private Job Babcock of Company F; Privates Peter E. Eldred, An
2 CONC drew W. Fish, Hale Henry and Dwight Parkhurst of Company A, Joseph Menney and John P. Sabin of Company D; and 34 enlisted men wounded.
2 CONT
2 CONT October-December	Companies A, B, D and F , Duty at Kernstown
2 CONT
2 CONT December 3-6	Companies A, B, D and F moved to Washington, D.C., then to Petersburg, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT December	Regiment reunited and assigned to Separate Brigade, Army of the James at Hart son’s Landing, Va. Company I detached at Fort Pocahontas.
2 CONT
2 CONT April 20	Private Daniel Cole of Company K killed by accidental explosion of shell 1865
2 CONT
2 CONT June 29	Mustered out at City Point, Va. under Colonel Robinson, Lt. Colonel McKinley and Major Ferguson. Recruits transferred to 96th New York Infantry.
2 CONT
2 CONT -------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT http://civilwarintheeast.com/us-regiments-batteries/new-york-infantry/184th-new-york/
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT 	 184th Infantry Regiment Civil War
2 CONT
2 CONT History The following is taken from New York in the War of the Rebellion, 3rd ed. Frederick Phisterer. Albany: J. B. Lyon Company, 1912.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mustered in: September 12, 1864 Mustered out: June 29, 1865
2 CONT
2 CONT This regiment, Col. Wardwell G. Robinson, was organized at Oswego, and mustered in the service of the United States for one year, at Elmira, September 12, 15 and 16, 1864. The few three years' men who were not to be mustered out w
2 CONC ith the regiment were transferred, June 27, 1865, to the 96th Infantry.
2 CONT
2 CONT The companies were recruited principally: A at Volney, Granby and Granger; B at Oswego, Scriba, Georgetown, DeRuyter and New Haven; C at Hannibal, Granby and Oswego; D at Oswego, Lebanon, Eaton, DeRuyter, Fenner and Mexico; E at V
2 CONC olney, Granby, Clarksville and Hannibal; F at Oswego; G at Sandy Creek, Richland, Boylston and Scriba; H at Hastings, Parish and West Monroe; I at Palermo, New Haven, Mexico, Hannibal and Constantia; and K at Schroeppel, Parish, W
2 CONC est Monroe, Fenner and Richland.
2 CONT
2 CONT Companies A, B, D and F, Maj. W. D. Ferguson, left the State September 12, 1864, and served in the 1st Brigade, 3d Division, 6th Corps, in the Army of the Shenandoah, from September, 1864; the other companies, Colonel Robinson, le
2 CONC ft the State September 16, 1864, and served at Bermuda Hundred, Army of the James; the regiment served in the Separate Brigade, Army of the James, at Harrison's Landing, Company I, at Fort Poca-hontas, Va., from December, 1864; an
2 CONC d, commanded by Colonel Robinson, it was honorably discharged and mustered out June 29, 1865, at City Point, Va.
2 CONT
2 CONT During its service the regiment lost by death, killed in action, 1 officer, 2 enlisted men; of wounds received in action, 8 enlisted men; of disease and other causes, 27 enlisted men; total, 1 officer, 37 enlisted men; aggregate, 
2 CONC 38; of whom 3 enlisted men died in the hands of the enemy.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT https://dmna.ny.gov/historic/reghist/civil/infantry/184thInf/184thInfMain.htm
