1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''John Sayre Bartlett'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/32121454/john_sayre_bartlett
2 CONT
2 CONT After platting the town of Marshall, Colonel William Beatty Archer (John's brother-in-law) secured a valuable beginning of the new community, in the settlement of John Bartlett and James Whitlock. John was a native of New York and
2 CONC  came to Walnut Prairie in 1817, but tired of country life and went to Chicago. Colonel Archer convinced him to come back to Marshall in 1836.
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Grave Inscription''
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bartlett Died Aug 16, 1865 aged 66y 9m 7d
2 CONT
2 CONT ''Gravesite Details''
2 CONT
2 CONT John is son of Revolutionary Soldier Ebenezer Seeley Bartlett & h/o Jane Archer
