1 NOTE DAR: The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution  Volume 19
2 CONT page 240 
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR: Mrs. Annie E. Beck.
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 18657 
2 CONT Born in St. Louis, Missouri. 
2 CONT Wife of John A. Beck. 
2 CONT Descendant of Capt. Richard Edsall, of New Jersey. 
2 CONT Daughter of William Aston McMurray and Catherine L. De Kay, his wife. 
2 CONT Granddaughter of William De Kay and Rachel Edsall, his wife. 
2 CONT Gr.-granddaughter of Richard Edsall and Jemima Seeley, his wife. 
2 CONT Richard Edsall, (1750-1823), was at the battles of Long Island, White  Plains, Brandywine, Germantown and Monmouth. He was commissioned  lieutenant, 1777, and on the death of his captain was promoted. At the  age of seventy he was
2 CONC  placed on the the pension roll of Sussex county for  service of lieutenant in the New Jersey Line. He was born in Hardyston  and died in Vernon township, N. J.
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR: The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution  Volume 19
2 CONT page 241 
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR: Mrs. Mary Danah Richardson.
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 18660 
2 CONT Born in St. Louis, Missouri. <BR>Wife of Joseph Clifford Richardson. 
2 CONT Descendant of Capt. Richard Edsall, of New Jersey. 
2 CONT Daughter of William Aston McMurray and Catherine L. De Kay, his wife 
2 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume  51
2 CONT page 21 
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR: [p.21] Mrs. Anne C. Burlingham.
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 50046 
2 CONT Born in N. Norwich, N. Y. 
2 CONT Wife of Holland Y. Burlingham. 
2 CONT Descendant of Capt. Jacobus Edsall. 
2 CONT Daughter of Dewitt Clinton Case and Irene Foote, his wife. 
2 CONT Granddaughter of Asa Foote and Almeda VandeGriff, his wife.  <BR>Gr-granddaughter of John VandeGriff and Almeda Edsall, his wife.  <BR>Gr-gr-granddaughter of Richard Edsall and Jemima Seely, his 2nd wife. 
2 CONT Gr-gr-gr-granddaughter of Jacobus Edsall and Charlotte Barton, his wife. 
2 CONT Jacobus Edsall (1726-1800) was captain in Col. Ephraim Martin's regiment,  Nathaniel Heard's brigade of New Jersey Continental line. He was born in  Bergen Co., N. J 
2 CONT The National Society of the Daughters of the American Revolution Volume  72
2 CONT page 106 
2 CONT
2 CONT DAR: Mrs. Katherine Lawrence Beck Heard.
2 CONT DAR ID Number: 71290 
2 CONT Born in St. Louis, Mo. <BR>Wife of Augustine A. Heard. 
2 CONT Descendant of Capt. Richard Edsall of New Jersey. 
2 CONT Daughter of John A. Beck and Annie E. McMurray, his wife. 
2 CONT Granddaughter of William A. McMurray and Catherine L. DeKay, his wife.  <BR>Gr-granddaughter of William De Kay and Rachel Edsall, his wife. 
2 CONT Gr-gr-granddaughter of Richard Edsall and Jemima Seeley, his wife. 
2 CONT Richard Edsall (1750-1823) was engaged in the battles of Long Island,  White Plains, Brandywine, Germantown, and Monmouth. He was commissioned  lieutenant, 1777, and on the death of his captain was promoted. At the  age of seventy
2 CONC  he was placed on the pension roll of Sussex County for  service as lieutenant, New Jersey Line. He was born in Hardyston; died in  Vernon, N. J.  
2 CONT
