1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Norton Claypole (1640-1688) emigrated to North America in 1678 and died there in Sussex County, Delaware.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Flag of England
2 CONT Norton Claypoole migrated from England to Colonial America.
2 CONT Flag of Colonial America
2 CONT
2 CONT Norton was a Friend (Quaker)
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Claypoole-29
2 CONT
2 CONT Norton was Justice of the Peace appointed by William Penn 25 of December 1682. [1][2] He was a prominent man in Delaware serving as a juryman, Clerk, Deputy Register, and served in Council for the Assembly.[1] In open court in May
2 CONC  of 1688, he traded with the Christian the Indian Sacamacko for 1000 acres of land.[1][3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT Norton was born to John Claypoole and Mary Angell about 1640.[4][5][6][7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Immigration
2 CONT 22 Feb 1678, on the Bachelor's Delight Norton migrated from England to Colonial America, settling in Lewes, Delaware.[4][6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Family Life
2 CONT In 1670, married Rachel (unknown maiden name).[5][6][8]
2 CONT
2 CONT # John b. 1672[9]
2 CONT # James b. 1673[4][5][10]
2 CONT # Mary b. 5 Aug 1682[1][4][5]
2 CONT # Robert b. 26 Nov 1683[1][4][5]
2 CONT # Jeremiah b. 23 Dec 1685[4][5][11]
2 CONT # Elizabeth b. 16 May 1687 [5][12][13]
2 CONT
2 CONT Religion
2 CONT Norton and Rachel were part of the Quaker group in Lewes, Delaware.[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death/Will
2 CONT Norton died in 1688.[1][4][6][14]
2 CONT
2 CONT Research Notes
