1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =John Lowry, Sr.=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John Lowry, Sr. Big Ydna Results, I-BY19889, - Scot - Irish'''
2 CONT * [https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_clans_and_septs_in_Ulaid '''List of clans and septs in Ulaid''']
2 CONT * [https://blog.nationalgeographic.org/2013/11/21/the-genographic-project-returns-to-ireland-to-reveal-dna-results/ ''The Genographic Project Returns to Ireland to Reveal DNA Results:''] The maternal DNA results showed great genet
2 CONC ic diversity, including lineages that dated back to some of the island’s earliest settlers (haplogroups U4.U5.U8), and some others that arrived more recently (haplogroups I, T1). The paternal DNA lineages were less diverse (88% of
2 CONC  participants were haplogroup R1b), likely a result of the dominance of a few male leaders like King Niall of the Nine hostages, as well as the historical influence of the Viking raids from across the North Sea.'''  
2 CONT * Son of William Lowry and Mary (Polly) Norris 
2 CONT * Born: August 10, 1799, in Robinson County, Tennessee, United States
2 CONT * Death:	January 07, 1867 (67) in Manti, Sanpete County, Utah, United States
2 CONT * Place of Burial: Manti Cemetery, Manti, Sanpete, Utah, United States
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/42881297 '''John Lowry, Sr. Find A Grave Memorial''']
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000014138904396&photo_id=6000000104087135821&position=1 '''John Lowry the son of William Lowry of Nashville,Tennessee and Mary Polly Norris is listed on John Lowry 
2 CONC Head Stone''']
2 CONT * Notes: Appointed to assist Andrew H. Perkins in presiding over the six missionaries assigned to Missouri for the purpose of assisting Joseph Smith's presidential campaign and to preach the gospel.  (History journal April 15, 184
2 CONC 4, p.2) Marital status: FamilySearch Priesthood office: High Priests Record pg.80
2 CONT * Served in Northern States Mission in 1843 (Age 43), Mission Type: Proselytizing, Marital Status: Married Priesthood Office: High-priest, Mission location and type: Journal History July 3 pg.1, 1843. Purpose was to preach the gos
2 CONC pel and "disabuse the public mind with regard to" Joseph Smith's arrest.  Priesthood office: High Priests Record pg.80
2 CONT * Served in Joseph Smith Presidential Campaign Mission in 1844 April 15–January (Age 44), Mission Type: Proselytizing
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000014138904396?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000176944345098 '''John Lowry (age 61) listed in 1860 Manti Sanpete, United States Federal Census''']
2 CONT * John Lowry  (age 51) listed in the 1850 Sanpete, Utah Territory, United States Federal Census
2 CONT
2 CONT =Immigrated to Utah in 1847=
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://history.lds.org/missionary/individual/john-lowry-1799?lang=eng John Lowry came to Utah on September 30, 1847 in the John Taylor Company]
2 CONT
2 CONT =Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868=
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lowry, Birth Date: 10 Aug. 1799, Death Date: 7 Jan. 1867, Age: 47 at time of crossing, Company: Edward Hunter - Jacob Foutz Company (1847), Departure: 19 June 1847, Arrival: 1 October 1847.  Company Information:
2 CONT 155 individuals and 59 wagons were in the company when it began its journey from the outfitting post on the Elkhorn River about 27 miles west of Winter Quarters, Nebraska.  Pioneer Information:  Captain of 5th Ten. His name and tr
2 CONC avel are mentioned in his daughter's obituary.
2 CONT
2 CONT John was first counselor to Bishop Hunter, the first bishop of Salt Lake City; also bishop of second ward, Salt Lake City, 1849; first bishop of Manti 1850.  Justice of peace at Manti.  Farmer and stockraiser.  Sent with John Craw
2 CONC ford, by Brigham Young, to colonize Elk Mountain country, Nevada.  Died Jan. 7,1867, in Manti, Utah. Headstone Inscription:  2D Lt Utah Territory Militia Indian Wars, Originally Created by: Dawnetta, Record added: Oct 09, 2009, Fi
2 CONC nd A Grave Memorial# 42881297
2 CONT
2 CONT John Lowry Sr., Captain of 5th Ten, both his name and travel are mentioned in his daughter's obituary.  John Lowry Sr. traveled in the Edward Hunter - Jacob Foutz Company (1847)
2 CONT
2 CONT Age at Departure: 47 and Head of Household
2 CONT
