1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From a family history written about Hyrum's brother John Lowry Jr. It states: "The Lowry family traveled on to the Missouri River, arriving there after the Mormon Batalion had been mustered out at Council Bluffs. T
2 CONC hey crossed the river to the west side at Winter Quarters and hastily built a house for the family and corrals for the cattle and prepared to stay there during the winter. Hearing of a place some distance up the river called Rush 
2 CONC Valley, where there was good feed for stock, Grandfather (John Lowry Sr.) took a herd of cattle up there to care for them during the winter; he also took father (John Lowry Jr.) and one other son to assist in the work, leaving Hyr
2 CONC um to assist the family at home...When grandfather and his two sons returned in the spring of 1847, they learned at that time that Hyrum, had attempted to cross the Missouri River to visit his Grandmother; he got lost and drowned.
2 CONC .."
2 CONT * Updated from [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=76548459 Find A Grave Memorial] via brother [http://www.geni.com/profile-34673577176 John Lowry, Jr] by [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartC
