1 NOTE {geni:about_me} OBITUARY -- The Manti Messenger, Friday 22 April 1910:  Death of Mary L. Peacock -- Mary Lowry Peacock wife of late Judge George Peacock died in Sterling Sunday after an illness of several weeks, at the home of her
2 CONC  son John L. Peacock.  She was one of the oldest settlers in that place and was the mother of ten children. She was a sister of John Lowry, a Manti pioneer now a resident of Springville. She was born in Missouri in November, 1834,
2 CONC  and came to Utah with her parents in 184?. The funeral was held from the Manti Tabernacle Wednesday and a large crowd of friends and relatives attended. 
2 CONT
