1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Justus Wellington Seeley''', son of Justus Azel Seely and Mehitable Bennett, was born January 30, 1815, Pickering, Canada. Came to Utah September, 1847, John Taylor company. Family home Mt. Pleasant, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Settled at Mt. Pleasant 1859. Justice of peace at Mt. Pleasant 20 years, member city council 1877-81 and 1883. Member ward bishopric 20 years. Farmer. Died April 28, 1894, at Mt. Pleasant.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Marriages and Children==
2 CONT #'''Clarissa Jane Wilcox'''  (daughter of Hazard Wilcox. Jr. and Sarah Seely of Charleston, Iowa, pioneers September 29, 1847, John Taylor company), married March 10, 1842, Charleston, Iowa. She was born October 1, 1821; came to U
2 CONC tah with husband in 1847. Their children:
2 CONT ##Orange born February 20, 1843, married Hannah Olsen;
2 CONT ##Sarah born April 10, 1844, married W. J. Tidwell;
2 CONT ##Don Carlos born January 4, 1846, married Hannah E. Reynolds
2 CONT ##Hyrum born March 29, 1848, married Mary E. Goldsbrough;
2 CONT ##Justus Wellington born June 25, 1850, married Annie E. Reynolds;
2 CONT ##William Hazard born October 25, 1852, married Charlotte Reynolds;
2 CONT ##John Henry born April 29, 1855, married Margaret Peel January 15, 1880;
2 CONT ##Mary Miranda born June 25, 1857, married Christian F. Peel;
2 CONT ##Joseph born March 30, 1862, married Sarah H. Allen;
2 CONT ##Stuart Randolph born February 16, 1865, married Millie Nielsen.
2 CONT #'''Sarah Jane McKinney'''  (daughter of William McKinney and Sarah Wilcox) who was born December 23, 1837, in Lewis county, Missouri, married November 17, 1873. Salt Lake City. Only child:
2 CONT ##Eva Rebecca born December 6, 1874, married Jens Christian Christensen.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Sources==
2 CONT *Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah photographs, page 109
2 CONT *Pioneers and Prominent Men of Utah, page 1152
