2 CONT === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT == Biography ==
2 CONT Sarah Tuttle Slawson
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Origins===Sarah was baptized in April, 1642 at New Haven, Connecticut Colony[NHChR 11].<ref name="PGM"/>  She was a daughter of [[Tuttle-27|William Tuttle]] and [[UNKNOWN-10582|Elizabeth UNKNOWN]].<ref name="PGM"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family===Sarah married John Slawson, son of George Slawson, on November 17, 1663 at New Haven.[NHVR 1:20]<ref name="PGM">Anderson, Robert C., [http://www.americanancestors.org/PageDetail.aspx?recordId=235840213 ''Great Migratio
2 CONC n 1634-1635, T-Y.''] (Pg 142) (Online database. AmericanAncestors.org. New England Historic Genealogical Society, 2012.) New EnglandHistoric Genealogical Society, 2011, accessed online May 8, 2014</ref><ref name="Slaw"/>
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Sarah and John Slawson:<ref name="Slaw"/># John Slauson b Sept 9, 1664 Stamford, Fairfield Co., mar Mary Holmes, daughter of Stephen and Martha. # Sarah Slason b Jan 20, 1667 Stamford, Fairfield Co.,  mar Ebenezer Bish
2 CONC op# Jonathan Slawson b July 25, 1670 Stamford, Fairfield Co., mar 1) Mary Waterbury, daughter of John and Mary, 2) Rose Stevens, daughter of Obadiah and Rebecca. # Elizabeth Slason b June 30, 1672 Stamford, Fairfield Co., mar Nath
2 CONC aniel Pond. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Death and Legacy===Sarah was killed on November 17, 1676 by her brother, Benjamin Tuttle,with an axe.  He was tried and hanged for the crime in 1677.<ref name="Slaw">Slawson, George C., comp. [https://archive.org/stream/slasons
2 CONC lausonsla00slaw#page/n3/mode/2up ''The Slason, Slauson, Slawson, Slosson family'']. Waverly, N.Y: Waverly sun, inc., 1946, accessed online May 7, 2014</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT == Sources ==
