1 NAME Richard Chamberlain /Mott/
2 GIVN Richard Chamberlain
2 SURN Mott
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 17 SEP 1815
2 PLAC Brockville, Leeds Greville, Ontario, Canada
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 13 NOV 1899
2 PLAC Grove, Cass, Iowa, USA
2 ADDR
1 BURI
2 DATE 15 NOV 1899
2 PLAC Atlantic, Cass County, Iowa, United States of America
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT from the Atlantic Daily Telegraph, Tuesday, November 14, 1899
2 CONT
2 CONT Death of Richard Mott.
2 CONT Richard Mott died last night at eight o'clock at his home some five miles south of this city on the Laurel street road; he was aged 84 years.  His death was not due to any specific disease but to the general breaking down of the s
2 CONC ystem due to his extreme old age.  The deceased has been a resident of this county for twenty years, residing in Brighton township for about half that period, and about ten years ago he purchased the old Watson farm on Turkey cree
2 CONC k, where he has resided ever since.  He leaves eight children, three sons and five daughters.  Four of them, H. A. Mott, Mrs. Frank Herbert, Mrs. Geo. Pellett and Mrs. O.W. Peterson reside in or near this city; Mrs. W. M. Mick in 
2 CONC Wayne county, Neb., Mrs. Lucy Wood and Geo. Mott in Wisconson, the former at Peshtigo and Joseph Mott in Canada.  The funeral services will be held tomorrow afternoon at one o'clock from the late residence and the remains interred
2 CONC  in the Atlantic cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT ***the 1880 census for Richard Mott indicates both his father and mother were born in Massachusetts, they were likely United Empire Loyalists (UEL, loyal to Great Britain), or children of UEL, who fled to Canada during or after th
2 CONC e American Revolution***
2 CONT
2 CONT ***Richard's tombstone indicates he was born in 1818, the above obituary indicates the year 1815***
2 CONT
2 CONT ***it is presumed that Jonathan Mott was the father of Richard Chamberlain Mott based on two items:
2 CONT 1) Jonathan had several dealings with a man named Richard Chamberlain in Leeds, Ontario in the early 19th century and had a son born about the time that Richard Chamberlain Mott was born
2 CONT 2) DNA connection exists between descendants of Richard Chamberlain Mott and descendants of Adam Mott, the ggg-grandfather of Jonathan Mott and the original Mott settler in the New World***
