1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * The information for Zachariah Lewis Webb is from Fine, Paul Alan, ''A River of Many Streams - The Ascendants and Descendants of Harry Anacker and Kathryn Allen''. Minnetonka, MN: RR Donnelly & Company, 2013, page
2 CONC  133.
2 CONT * Zachariah was a graduate in law. He was a founding member and Junior Warden at the Church of the Redeemer in Addison, New York in 1854; a Justice of Sessions in Steuben County, New York in 1855, and a Justice of the Peace in Cor
2 CONC ning, Steuben County, New York in 1860.
2 CONT * As of July 1850, the Webb family---Zachariah, Polly, Ann, Catherine, and Lewis---was residing in Marshall, Calhoun County, Michigan.
2 CONT * Zachary was a merchant. The Webbs lived in Marshall between Abigail’s birth in Steuben County, New York in September 1848 and Ellen’s birth in Steuben County, New York in November 1853.
2 CONT * Zachariah owned a considerable amount of land in the city of Auburn. He was a Knight Templar in St. Paul’s Lodge No. 124 F and A.M. of the Masons, and of the Salem Town Commandery. As of 9 February 1854 Zachariah was King of the
2 CONC  Addison, New York Chapter No. 146of the Royal Arch Masons.
2 CONT * Zachariah and his brother-in-law George Curtiss Williams held a contract at Auburn Prison for shoemaking, for which they employed 41 men. The contract expired 1 May 1835.
