1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Townsend McCoun'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/144936269/townsend-mccoun Find A Grave Memorial ID # 144936269]
2 CONT
2 CONT ''President of Troy Savings Bank in 1824''
2 CONT
2 CONT Townsend McCoun, b. Jan. 31, 1769, m. at Nassau, New York, b. February 21, 1794, Sarah Vail, b. October 2, 1775 (daughter of Moses Vail of Washington, New York and Phoebe Holmes. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Aaron, father of Moses Vail, was a noted Quaker preacher in Duchess County, New York) He was a merchant in Troy, where he lived for forty years (1794-1834), much respected for his good sense, integrity and benevolence and for his 
2 CONC enterprise and public spirit, and was one of the most prominent men of his day in Troy. He died September 21, 1834, age. 65. His widow resided still jn Troy, in 1869, age. 93. 
2 CONT
2 CONT They had four children.
