1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Sarah McCoun Gould (Vail)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/250017014/sarah-gould Find A Grave Memorial ID # 250017014] 
2 CONT * [https://lansingburghhistoricalsocietyarchives.org/the-village/blocks-buildings-etc/oaklands/ Oaklands Estate]
2 CONT
2 CONT She was the daughter of George and Jane (Thomas) Vail, of Troy, New York. Attended Troy Seminary from 1832 to 1838. Married Chief Justice George Gould, of Troy. Continuous residence, “Oaklands,” Troy, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT Emma Willard and Her Pupils: Or, Fifty Years of Troy Female Seminary, 1822-1872. Mrs. Russell Sage, 1898. 248.
2 CONT
2 CONT —The funeral of Mrs. Sarah McCoun Vail Gould, whose death occurred Sunday, will be held from her late residence, “Oaklands,” at the head of [One Hundred] Third street, Lansingburgh, to-morrow morning at 10:30 o’clock. Rev. Dr. Edg
2 CONC ar A. Enos of St. Paul’s Church, of which the deceased was a member, will officiate. The bearers will be John I. Thompson, George T. Lane, A. C. Comstock, C. W. Tillinghast, Thomas Buckley and William Henry Warren. The interment w
2 CONC ill be in the George Vail mortuary at Oakwood cemetery. “Obituary.” Troy Daily Times. August 29, 1899: 3 col 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT TO RENT—Oaklands, Fifth Avenue and [One Hundred] Third Street, Lansingburgh, the residence of the late Mrs. S. M. Gould. House with all modern improvements; conservatory and green houses attached; good outbuildings; fine grounds; 
2 CONC a large variety of fruit trees and flowers, with twenty-five acres of land; only fifteen minutes’ ride from the centre of the city. Apply to THOMAS E. NEWBOLD, on the premises, or W. W. ROUSSEAU, JR., 257 Broadway. 3-5-4t “To Let.
2 CONC ” Troy Daily Times. March 9, 1900: col 8.
2 CONT
2 CONT —The Junior League of Hedding Methodist Church will hold a musical and literary social at “Oaklands,” formerly the old Gould property, on the evening of November 28.
2 CONT
2 CONT —Edward O’Neil and William Riley have been awarded the contract for building catchbasins on the Gould property, recently purchased by Edward Murphy, 2d, and through which streets are being opened “Lansingburgh.” Troy Daily Times. 
2 CONC November 21, 1900: 4 col 5.
2 CONT
2 CONT —Complaint was made to Commissioner of Public Safety Coyle Saturday afternoon of a building moved from the Gould property at [One Hundred] Third Street and Fifth Avenue and allowed to stand on Fifth Avenue, near [One Hundred] Fift
2 CONC h Street. The Commissioner directed Captain Kirkpatrick to have it removed, and Officer Rowe was detailed. It was found that C. Augustus Roemer, who purchased the building is moving the building to his property on [One Hundred] Tw
2 CONC enty-third Street. He had secured a permit from Commissioner of Public Works Phelan. He was directed to remove the building from the street as quickly as possible, as it is a menace to travel on the thoroughfare “Upper Troy.” Troy
2 CONC  Daily Times. January 14, 1901: 3 col 5.
2 CONT
2 CONT —The Sunday School class of Mrs. Alice Dusenberry of Hedding Methodist Church will enjoy a lawn festival Wednesday evening at Oaklands, south of the church. “Upper Troy.” Troy Daily Times. June 3, 1901: 4 col 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT —The house which was formerly the family residence of Mrs. Tracy Gould has been purchased from Edward Murphy, 2d, by contractor Walter Mott, who will move it to the corner of [One Hundred] Third Street and Sixth Avenue and will re
2 CONC model it. “Upper Troy.” Troy Daily Times. March 20, 1902: col 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT Roemer Charles A civil engineer 509 Frear bldg and instructor R P I h 19 [One Hundred] Twenty-third Lans
2 CONT Directory of Troy, Watervliet and Green Island, Cohoes and Waterford NY. Vol. 79. Albany, NY: Sampson & Murdock, 1907. 408.
2 CONT
2 CONT * [http://www.litchfieldhistoricalsociety.org/ledger/students/1043 George Gould. Litchfield Historical Society, Litchfield Law School]
2 CONT * [https://artgallery.yale.edu/collections/objects/479 Judge George Gould. Yale University Art Gallery]
2 CONT * [https://books.google.com/books?id=5rUEAAAAYAAJ Gould, Sarah McCoun Vail. Memorial of Judge George Gould. Troy, NY: William H. Young & Blake, 1871]
