3 CITY Syracuse
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 23 OCT 1830
2 ADDR
3 CITY Owego
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 5 OCT 1896
2 ADDR
3 CITY Syracuse
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU Silversmith
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Death of Orlando P. Curry
2 CONT
2 CONT Orlando P. Curry, a well known resident of this city, died at his home No. 802 Almond street, at noon yesterday. He was 58 years of age, and was a silversmith by occupation, for 30 years being in the employ of A.H. Schrender. Mr. 
2 CONC Curry came to Syracuse from Owego in 1864. He is survived by a wife and seven children, viz: Mrs. C.e. White of Bedford, D.; Mrs T.C. Robinson, Charles H., Edwin H., William P., George D., and Albert Curry. Mr. Curry was a member 
2 CONC of the Fourth Baptist church and had been instrumental in founding several of the younger Baptist churches in this city.
2 CONT
2 CONT Syracuse Daily Standard, October 6, 1896 Page 6
