2 CONT 2nd wife: Sally Peck Bishop married Henderson, NY. married Jan. 19, 1817 Henderson, Jefferson, NY. (had 12 children).
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/91692970/calvin-bishop Find a Grave appears to be incorrect regarding his mother, who is Serviah Bishop. Her name is also incorrectly stated as Sophia on FAG.
2 CONT
2 CONT From Find a Grave Contributor:
2 CONT
2 CONT A veteran of 1812, his name appears on a muster roll of a company of infantry commanded by Captain George W. Clark in a regiment commanded by Lieut. Col. Anthony Sprague, ordered into service by Brig. Gen. Jacob Brown, now in the 
2 CONC service of the United States.
2 CONT
2 CONT From an anonymous email by a nonmember;
2 CONT
2 CONT Calvin Bishop was born 9 February 1782 at Chesterfield, Cheshire, New Hampshire a son of John and Experience Harris Bishop. He died at Henderson, Jefferson, New York, 24 January 1850 of consumption. He had a total of eighteen chil
2 CONC dren, six by his first wife, Sally Mary Armstrong, and twelve by his second wife Sally Peck. A large number of this family died of consumption, so he has fewer descendants than you would expect froom this large family.
