1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Mormon Pioneer Overland Travel, 1847–1868==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Fisher, Elizabeth Jane'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth Date: 	9 Feb. 1839
2 CONT Death Date: 	12 Dec. 1885 Gender: 	Female Age: 	11 Company: 	Gilbert and Gerrish Freight Train (1850)
2 CONT
2 CONT >SOURCE: http://lds.org/churchhistory/library/pioneerdetails/1,15791,4018-1-46301,00.html
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Great Salt Lake, Utah Territory - 1850
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Salt Lake, Utah Territory, United States - 1860
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Relation to Head of House: Wife, Skaneateles, Onondaga, New York, USA - June 1 1875
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Marital Status: MarriedRelation to Head of House: Wife, East Mill Creek, Salt Lake, Utah, USA - 1880
2 CONT *
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Fourth of seven children of Joseph Fisher and Evaline McLean. Came with her family from Nauvoo to Utah in one of the earliest pioneer companies, settling in East Mill Creek. Married [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=g
2 CONC r&GRid=22199633 Isaac Joseph Seely] 17 May 1862 in Salt Lake City. They had eight children, of whom the sixth was [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=seely&GScid=77162&GRid=21740126& Arta McLean Seely].
