1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Death of Mr. I. D. Smith Died in Constantine, Wednesday, Nov. 1, 1882, of typhoid fever after an illness of two weeks, Mr. Isaac D. Smith. The deceased was born in Charlotteville, Canada, December 1, 1828. At the a
2 CONC ge of 29 he heard the call of the Great Master, and accepted the divine invitation of mercy, and soon after became a member of the Baptist church at Forrestville, Canada. In 1866, he moved to Plainwell, Michigan, where he lived te
2 CONC n or eleven years; then he with his family found a home four years at Falesburg, Illinois, from which place he removed to Constantine one year ago last May, where as a artist he was so well and favorably known. Mr. Smith was first
2 CONC  married to Miss Abigail Mabee in 1852, who died in 1857, leaving three little ones alone to the father's care. In 1858, Miss Sarah Johnson, his now bereaved companion undertook the delicate responsibility of sharing that care. bu
2 CONC t now after more than twenty-four years are gone, the loyed father is taken, leaving four other children to mingle their tears and grief with the other surviving friends.  The funeral service are to be held at the residence at 2 o
2 CONC 'clock Saturday afternoon.
2 CONT
