1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Obituary==
2 CONT Winchester, April 14 - (Special) - Charles B. Mabee died Friday and was buried Saturday afternoon. Mr. Mabee came to Monteagle from Canada when it was simply a small station called Moffet. He and his father were the first postmast
2 CONC ers at Monteagle. His mother is still living. He leaves a wife, married son, O. C. Mabee; two married daughters, Mrs. Crawford Douglas of Chattanooga and Mrs. Will Thompston of Bridgeport and several unmmarried children.
2 CONT The Nashville American, 15 April 1900, page 2<ref>https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/57593564/charles_byron-mabee/photo</ref>
2 CONT
2 CONT * Find a Grave, database and images (https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/57593564/charles_byron-mabee: accessed September 9, 2025), memorial page for Charles Byron Mabee (1856–14 Apr 1900), Find a Grave Memorial ID 57593564, citin
2 CONC g Monteagle Cemetery, Monteagle, Marion County, Tennessee, USA; Maintained by forrester3K (contributor 47351279).
2 CONT
