1 NOTE {geni:about_me} D/O Donald Fraser and Isabella Ross
2 CONT
2 CONT Ellen Gustin
2 CONT
2 CONT One of Bosanquet Township's pioneers died Friday afternoon, Jan. 4, 1929, in the person of Mrs. Charles Gustin in her 85th year.
2 CONT
2 CONT Her maiden name was Ellen Fraser, and she was twice married, her first husband being Keil (Achilles) Lapham, of Bosanquet, and her second husband Charles Gustin Sr. also of Bosanquet who predeceased her by about 16 years.
2 CONT
2 CONT There are two brothers and one sister survives, John Fraser, & Mrs. Rebecca Brand of Forest, and William Fraser of Bosanquet at whose home she died. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The funeral will be held on Sun. afternoon from Wm. Fraser residence to the Lake Shore United Church where the service will be conducted by the Rev. W. L. Hiles of the Forest United Church. Interment will be made in Ravenswood Cem
2 CONC etery.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=50570572 Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''May 31 2017, 19:41:30 UTC''
