1 NOTE {geni:about_me} SAXMAN-Willlam H. Smith, 93, died Saturday at the home of a daughter in Hutchinson after a year's illness. Born Jan. 23, 1871, at Farmington, Iowa, he moved to the Saxman community in 1876 and had farmed here since
2 CONC . He married Mary M. Baker Sept. 4, 1893 at Saxman. She died in 1949.
2 CONT Member: Saxman United Presbyterian Church.
2 CONT Survivors: Daughters, Mrs, Clara Wyatt, 708 East 8th, Hutchinson; Mrs. Hazel Donnelly, Lyons; Mrs. Nina Musterman, St. Louis, Mo.; Mrs, Jessie Bundy, Lyons; Mrs. Wllma Busley, Portland, Ore.; a son, Orvllle, Lyons; a foster-son, G
2 CONC eorge L., Nickerson; 8 grandchildren, 26 great - grandchildren and 9 great-greatgrandchildren.
2 CONT Funeral: 2 p.m. Tuesday, Crawford-Miller Mortuary, Lyons; Rev. John Stevenson. Burial: Lyons Cemetery. Call: 7-9 p.m. Monday at the mortuary.
2 CONT
2 CONT from The Hutchinson News
2 CONT Monday, 8 June 1964* Reference: [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/21363389/william-heaton-smith Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 9 2024, 23:50:35 UTC''
