1 NOTE 	1  UID 8BDFD3B0C5025340B5B08BE5CA286EFB77B5
2 CONT
2 CONT Flavius says she died in McLean, Illinois, not Haddam, Kansas. BK II, pg. 32 para 4 "Seedlings of William Foster".
2 CONT Informatin for Mary Foster and her Ancestors was retrived from information submitted by :
2 CONT Judith Kathleen Fowler
2 CONT 20100 Manzanita Drive
2 CONT Willits, CA  95490
2 CONT To the PEDIGREE RESOURCE FILE
2 CONT Submission Search: 63220-093099164849
2 CONT DISC # 6, Mary's PIN # 381244
2 CONT
2 CONT "Polly Mary, 2nd child of Harrison & Ann (Bartlett) Foster, born in Bourbon, KY, went with her parents to Clark County.  Here she met and married Dennis Foster, half-brother to James T.  They moved to Switzerland Co., Indiana, She
2 CONC lby Co., KY, and then to Hancock, Indiana, where they owned land.  Some of their children were born in each of these counties.  In 1842, Dennis sold the Indiana land and took his family to McLean Co., Illinois.  It seems the buy e
2 CONC r of the land couldn't make the payments, and the land was resold in late 1844.
2 CONT
2 CONT On Oct. 10, 1845, Dennis bought land from John R. Patton, pg. 139, in McLean, Ill.  When Dennis died, Polly's brothers, Harrison and Aaron Foster were appointed adminstrators of his estate, which included 165 acres of land.  Polly
2 CONC  and Dennis are buried in the Pleasant Hill cemetery, McLean Co., Illinois, but there is no tombstone." --"Seedlings of William Foster" by Flavius Foster, pg. 31
2 CONT
2 CONT Harrison Foster's will; it was probated July 26, 1819...  FOSTER, HARRISON  Weak in body. To eldest son William, one-sixth part of estate, after paying his son Aron $20.00. To eldest daughter Polley, one cow, one bed, and as much 
2 CONC more as will make her share equal with her brother William's. To son Aron, one-sixth part of estate. To daughter Pheby, one-sixth part of estate. To daughter Lettis, one-sixth part of estate. To youngest daughter Dorcas, 20 shilli
2 CONC ngs.  Executor: Brother Payton Foster. Witnesses: Thomas Berry, William Foster. Payton Foster qualified with William Foster as surety.
1 NOTE Husband and wife were probably cousins
