2 DATE 23 FEB 1902
2 PLAC Clark County, Illinois, USA
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Son of James Bartlett & Hannah M.(Tuladay) Bartlett. Husband of Sarah Ann (Smith) Bartlett.
2 CONT                 ~~~~~~~~~~~
2 CONT Warren Bartlett was born on the old Bartlett farm in Clark County, May 20, 1825 and died Sunday evening February 23, 1902, aged 76 years, 9 months and 3 days.  In 1847 he was married to Sarah Ann Smith.   Ten children were born to
2 CONC  them, seven sons and three daughters
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1849, he went with an ox team across the Great Plains to California to the gold fields. Returning he bought a farm upon which he still resides. In 1878 his wife died and his home has been presided over by his daughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT He joined the United Brethren Church in 1869. Funeral services were conducted by Rev. Cross at Potters Hall and he was laid to rest in the Plymouth Cemetery.
2 CONT
2 CONT Source:  Clark County Herald, 5 March 1902
2 CONT
2 CONT WARREN BARTLETT, farmer, P.O. West Union. Among the most successful farmers of Melrose Township may be mentioned Warren Bartlett. He is a native of Clark County, IL, born May 20, 1825 and raised within half a mile of his present h
2 CONC ome. Warren was given such educational advantages as were to be had, consisting of about three months each winter. He was married May 30, 1847, to Miss Sarah Ann Smith, daughter of John and Charlotte Smith. She was born in Ohio, M
2 CONC arch 7, 1825, and came to this county with her parents in 1846, and died here on the 2nd of August, 1878, leaving a family of ten children, of whom one is deceased. She was for several years a member of the Methodist Episcopal chu
2 CONC rch, and the last ten or twelve years was a member of the United Brethren Church. Devoted to her church and to her family, the loss in her death is felt by a large circle of friends, whose confidence and love she enjoyed in the fu
2 CONC llest degree, but more especially by her husband and family to whom she appears to have performed the office of a guardian angel. The record of the family is as follows: Delilah H., born June 4, 1848, married to Thomas J. Snavely;
2 CONC  Perry C. Bartlett, born September 8, 1851, married Miss Sarah Janney, two children, viz.: Ethelbert and Avery B. Bartlett; Charlotte M., born June 23, 1853, married Jeremiah Grant, and died November, 1876, leaving two children, v
2 CONC iz: Edward Grant and Nellie F. Grant, the former in the family of Joseph Smith, and the latter a member of subject's family; Martha A. Bartlett, born January 30, 1855; Jefferson Bartlett, born April 7, 1857; Iredell Bartlett, born
2 CONC  February 2, 1859; Warren, born May 6, 1861, married to Mary J. Scott, widow of James Scott, and the daughter of James W. and Mary J. Boyles, one child, Dora May Scott; Joseph Bartlett, born December 14, 1862; William N. Bartlett,
2 CONC  born October 7, 1865; Edward E. Bartlett, born August 18, 1869. Mr. Warren Bartlett is a member of the United Brethren Church, and labors assiduously for the promotion of temperance or total abstinence.* Reference: [https://www.f
2 CONC indagrave.com/memorial/32006328/warren-bartlett Find A Grave Memorial] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 16 2024, 10:43:48 UTC''
