1 OCCU 10th Regiment, Michigan Cavalry, 5th Regiment, Michigan Cavalry
1 TITL Major General
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Major General Luther Stephen Trowbridge (USA)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/8150811/luther-stephen-trowbridge
2 CONT
2 CONT Luther Stephen Trowbridge joined the 5th Michigan Cavalry (part of Custer's Brigade) in 1862 as a Major. After seeing action at Gettysburg, he was promoted in 1863 to Lt. Colonel of the 10th Michigan Cavalry in which he became Col
2 CONC onel in 1864. He saw much action in the western theatre and at war's end was stationed in Tennessee where he took an active part in the pursuit of President Jefferson Davis. On September 1, 1865, he was breveted Major General in r
2 CONC ecognition of his service. He went to Yale College and practiced law in Detroit before the war. He married Julia Buel in 1862, the daughter of his law partner, former Michigan U.S. Congressman Alexander W. Buel
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Civil War Union Brevet Major General. Served during the Civil War first as the Major of the 5th Michigan Volunteer Cavalry, then as Colonel and commander of the 10th Michigan Volunteer Cavalry. He was brevetted both Brigadier and 
2 CONC Major General, U.S. Volunteers on June 15, 1865 for ''"faithful and meritorious services."''
2 CONT
2 CONT BATTLE UNIT NAME: 5th Regiment, Michigan Cavalry 
2 CONT SIDE: Union 
2 CONT COMPANY: F&S SOLDIER'S 
2 CONT RANK IN: Major SOLDIER'S 
2 CONT RANK OUT: Major 
2 CONT ALTERNATE NAME: 
2 CONT FILM NUMBER: M545 
2 CONT ROLL 43 
2 CONT PLAQUE NUMBER: 
