0 @I6000000167103640075@ INDI
1 NAME David Roe /Seely/
2 GIVN David Roe
2 SURN Seely
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 12 FEB 1826
2 PLAC Chester, Orange, New York
2 ADDR
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 JUL 1903
2 PLAC Chester, Orange, New York
2 ADDR
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT Names and dates taken from 2 family bibles.  The first was published in 1879 in New York and now belongs to Ruth Schulenburg of Stratford, Connecticut.  The second was published in 1889 in New York and now belongs to Karen Allen o
2 CONC f Shelton, Connecticut.   Both belonged to their mother, Ruth Dunning Seely Schulenburg, before she died.
2 CONT
2 CONT Orange County Surrogate Count Document (Book B, Page 191) dated 16 July 1831 shows David Roe Seely to be the son of Albert and Deborah Seely.  His age is shown as "five years the twelfth day of February" last past.
2 CONT
2 CONT The following is shown on page 122 of David Roe's will:  " I give and bequeath to my grandson David R. Seely the sum of three hundred dollars" . . . etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT David R. Seely's Letter of Administration dated 28 Aug 1903 is filed in the Orange County Surrogate Count Records in Book X, Page 416.  His daughter, Clara R. Seely, is designated to administer the disposal of his estate.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is listed in the SGS Vol. III as #3855 on Page 75.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hand written records received from the Warwick, New York cemetery on 15 May 2006 read as follows:  "David Seely , Born Chester, N.Y., Lived in Chester, N.Y., Age 77, Parents Albert Seely & Deborah Roe.  Died 7-1-1903."
