1 NAME Mary /unknown/ widow Mason
2 GIVN Mary
2 SURN unknown
2 NSFX widow Mason
2 _MARNM Seeley
2 NICK Mary (NN) [Heath] [Mason] widow of Mr. Health
2 NICK married Walter Mason; then married Robert Seeley as Mary (NN) Health Mason;
2 NICK Mary Mason
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE ABT 1580
2 PLAC of
2 ADDR
3 CITY London
3 STAE England
1 DEAT
2 DATE 10 MAR 1647
2 ADDR
3 CITY New Haven
3 STAE New Haven Colony
3 CTRY Colonial America
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mary must have been a remarkable woman. From the St. Stephen Coleman Street registers we learn that she was living in the parish as early as 1610, when her son Ambrose was baptized. Her first child was probably Reb
2 CONC ecca, who was buried in 1623. Since no baptism for Rebecca occurred at St. Stephen's, it is likely she was the first child and was baptized in the same parish where Mary and her first husband, William Heath, a weaver, were married
2 CONC . They had at least seven children before his death in 1620, one of them a stillbirth. One other child died before the father. While a widow, her children Judith and Ambrose Heath were buried, reducing her surviving children to th
2 CONC ree. About 1621 she married Walter Mason, also a weaver. Neither of her first two marriages took place at St. Stephen's and otherwise have not been found despite many searches.
2 CONT
2 CONT To Walter she bore at least three more children. While married to Walter, two more Heath children, Rebecca and Phillip, died, plus one of Walter's, and then on 1 Sep 1625, Mary attended the burial of not only Walter her husband bu
2 CONC t two more of her children, one a Heath and one a Mason. The number of burials each month at St. Stephen's Coleman Street in 1625 tells the story more completely: 16 in January, 3 in February, 11 March, 10 April, 5 May, 9 June, 78
2 CONC  July, 256 August, 93 September, 8 October, 8 November, and 6 December. Mary's family had been nearly wiped out by the plague. She was left with a single child, Elizabeth Mason, who was baptized 2 May 1624, but who also was buried
2 CONC  at St. Stephen's 14 Mar 1625/6.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.seeley-society.net/sgs-research-AlanJPhipps-RobertSeeley.html ____________________________
2 CONT
2 CONT Robert and Mary HEATH were married 15 Dec 1626 at London, England. She was b. 1589/90 in England and d. 1630 in England. Robert immigrated to America, apparently after her death. Robert and Mary MANNING were married 22 Dec 1666 at
2 CONC  Huntington, Long Island, NY. She was b. 1620 in England and d. in NY. Her father was William MANNING. I'd guess Robert met his second wife in NY. The CASTLE family gedcom shows Robert's b. in 1600.
2 CONT --------------------
