1 OCCU London Lawyer; Merchant-politician, Elected MP for Bossinney
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Thomas Povey''' (b. 1613/14, d. in or before 1705) FRS, was a London merchant-politician who was active in colonial affairs from the 1650s, but neutral enough in his politics to be named a member from 1660 of Ch
2 CONC arles II's Council for Foreign Plantations, making him a powerful figure in the not-yet professionalised First English Empire, both "England's first colonial civil servant" and at the same time "a typical office holder of the Rest
2 CONC oration".[3] Both Samuel Pepys and William Berkeley Governor of Virginia, railed at times against Povey's incompetence and maladministration.<br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thomas_Povey
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary, daughter of John Adderly and widow of John Agard of King's Bromley, Staffordshire.
2 CONT
