1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sailed on the ship "Amity" from Downs for Pennsylvania, February 23, 1682, as assistant to William Penn's surveyor, Captain Thomas Holmes.  Commenting on his son's appointment as surveyor, the elder Claypoole remar
2 CONC ked with wisdom, "In a few years his occupation may become profitable.  However, it will be a present maintenance and keep him from ill company."  He was clerk of the Colonial Assembly from 1686 to 1690; collector of Supply Money 
2 CONC for Philadelphia; appointed as High Sheriff of Philadelphia in 1687 and again in 1693.  
