1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT ===James Claypoole II
2 CONT *Birth:  Jun. 12, 1664 - London, Middlesex, England
2 CONT * Death:  Jul. 24, 1706 -  Lewes, New Castle County, Delaware
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family    
2 CONT * Parents:   James Claypoole (1634 - 1687)   Helena Mercer Claypoole (1634 - 1688)  
2 CONT * Spouse:   Mary Cann Claypoole (1680 - 1705)  
2 CONT * Children:   James Claypool (1701 - 1789) married Jane Elizabeth Byrd
2 CONT * Siblings:   John Claypoole (1658 - 1700)*   Mary Claypoole Cooke (1660 - 1726)*   Helen Claypoole Bethell (1662 - 1691)*   James Claypoole (1664 - 1706)   Prissilla Claypoole Crappe (1666 - 1698)*   Nathaniel Claypoole (1668 - 1
2 CONC 668)*   Josiah Claypoole (1669 - 1670)*   Samuel Claypoole (1671 - 1681)*   Nathaniel Claypoole (1672 - 1714)*   Infant Son Claypoole (1673 - 1673)*   George Claypoole (1675 - 1731)*   Joseph Claypoole (1676 - 1676)*   Joseph Clay
2 CONC poole (1677 - 1741)*   Elizabeth Claypoole Pettyjohn (1687 - 1749)*  
2 CONT *Calculated relationship  
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT From: THE STILLE FAMILY IN AMERICA 1641 – 1772 Swedish American Genealogist - Vol. 6 No. 4 Dec 1986 By Peter Stebbins Craig
2 CONT
2 CONT >Notes [49] The first discovered reference to Christiern Steelman occurs in 1708 when (as a cordwainer or shoemaker) he is named husband of Mary, widow of James Claypoole, Jr., who had died in 1706 in New Castle County. DH, 5:278,
2 CONC  n. 19. James Claypoole, Jr. (1664-1706) had arrived in America on the Concord in 1683 with his parents, James Claypoole, Sr. (1634-1687) and his wife Helena (Mercer) Claypoole (d. 1688), close personal friends of William Penn. PW
2 CONC P, 2:369-373. On 22 Dec. 1701, before the Pennsylvania Board of Property, James Claypoole, Jr., testified that his wife’s mother (being also the mother of Adam Peterson) had been murdered by Indians thirty years before. PA, 2d Ser
2 CONC ., 19:221-2, 224. From this we may infer that James Claypoole, Jr.’s wife (and the wife of Christiern Steelman) was Mary Peterson, of Swedish or Dutch parentage. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
