1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Unknown-242157
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Rachel''', surname at birth unknown, was the wife of Norton Claypoole. She married her husband in St. Alfege Parish, Greenwich, Kent, England on 12 July 1670.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT Norton and Rachel Claypoole had
2 CONT
2 CONT # John Claypoole
2 CONT # James Claypoole
2 CONT # Mary Claypoole
2 CONT # Robert Claypoole
2 CONT # Jeremiah Claypoole
2 CONT # Elizabeth Claypoole
2 CONT
2 CONT Their first two children were born in England:
2 CONT
2 CONT * John Claypoole, 1672 [2]
2 CONT * James Claypoole, 1673[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT The couple subsequently immigrated to British Colonial America. We first see Rachell Claypoole giving birth to her children, Mary and Robert Claypoole in Sussex County, Delaware.
2 CONT
2 CONT "Mary Claypoole, the daughter of Norton and Rachel Claypoole, was "borne aboute the 1st Houre in the morning 10th day of the 8th Month 1682 in the presence of Edward Sowthorns wife the midwife, Katherine Hews, & her daughter Eliza
2 CONC beth, Honor Clark, jonica Wiltbanck, Margarett Molleston, Sewsanna Grey, Sarah Stretcher, Sarah Bartlett”[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Robert the son of Norton & Rachell Claypoole borne the 26th day of the 11th Month 1683 about the 11th houre at night in the presence of Elizabeth the wife of Simon Pawlin the midwife Susanna the wife of Dennis ffisher & Elizabeth
2 CONC  Tompson oure maid servant."[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT On 24 June 1685, Rachel served as a witness to the marriage of George Young and the widow Mary Southrin in Lewes.[6]
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Jeremiah was born six months later in Dec 1685[7]
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1687, Rachel gave birth to a daughter, Elizabeth:[8]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Elizabeth, daugher of Norton and Rachell Claypoole, was born at Lewis [Lewes], Delaware, 16 3rd mo. 1687 about 7 P.M. 'in the presence of Thomas Wynne and Elizabeth his wife, ye midwife, & Jane Maud, her daughter, Hannah Bailey..
2 CONC ."
2 CONT
2 CONT A few months later, Rachell and her husband hosted a marriage of Jane Maude and Isaac Bowde. Rachell was one of the witnesses to the marriage.
2 CONT
2 CONT ”Marriage of Isack Bowd late of Philadelphia single man to Jane Mawde of Lewis single woman of spinster. September 15, 1687 in the house of Norton Claypoole. Robt. Clifton, Justice of the Peace; Norton Claypoole, Clerk & Register.
2 CONC  [Witnesses]: John Wynne, Adam Johnson, Henry Mollestine, John Millington, Step. Sargent, Sam. Pope, Nehemiah ffield, Johannis Winster, Joseph Alef [Allis], Mathew M. Osborne, Sarah Screcther M., Sarah N. Russell, Mary MOC Mollest
2 CONC on, Margaret Mollestine, Rachell Claypoole.”[9]
2 CONT
2 CONT Within the next year, Norton Claypoole died. In September 1688, the widowed Rachel administered her husband's estate:[10]
2 CONT
2 CONT (Court Sitting June 5th, 6th, 8th 1688
2 CONT “Upon ye 16th Day of the Sixth Month 1688, Rachel Claypoole Widdow Having Desired Luke Watson Senr and Thomas Oldman to bee Appraisers of ye Goods and Chattells Now in her possession, being ye Goods & Chattells of her Late Husband
2 CONC  Norton Claypoole (Deceased)…”
2 CONT “Rachel Claypoole (Widdow) being Attested to Bring in a True acot of ye Estate Goods and Chattells of Norton Claypoole her husband Deceased did Give in an Inventorie of ye same Beaering Date as abovesaid To ye best of her knowledg
2 CONC e As will appear by ye said Inventorie.
2 CONT “Reserving to her Selfe One Bed and furniture Together with waireing apparell and ye Plantacon She lives on”
2 CONT
2 CONT She subsequently married Nehemiah Field in 1689.[11]
2 CONT
2 CONT “Com: Sussex December the 6th 1689.
2 CONT “Lett this Certifie whom It may Concerne that Nehemiah ffield Batchelor and Rachel Claypoole widow Did * * * Take Each other as Husband and Wife etc.”
2 CONT “NEHEMIAH FIELD, RACHEL FIELD”[12]
2 CONT
2 CONT They had children Nehemiah Field and William Field:
2 CONT
2 CONT “Nehemiah the Son of Nehemiah and Rachel ffield Relicte of Norton Claypoole Deceased was borne on the Twentieth Day of December in the year One Thousand Six hundred Eighty and Nine. And his younger Brother William ffield Borne on 
2 CONC the Twenty fifty of December In the year One Thousand Six hundred Ninety and three.”[13]
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Research Notes
2 CONT
2 CONT Note As no record of their marriage in 1670 is found, Rachel's maiden name is not known. Rachel remarried Nehemiah Field after the death of Norton. They were married on December 6, 1689. Rachel sailed with their three year old son
2 CONC , James, from Gravesend, England to Delaware in June 1681 and arrived in September.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Sources
2 CONT ↑ London, England, Church of Eng
