2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000014661210096?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000207588969898 '''Abner Lowry Funeral Services''']
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/18934520/abner-lowry '''Abner Lowry, Jr. Find A Grave Memorial''']
2 CONT * [https://app.agencybloc.com/login.aspx?ReturnUrl=%2f '''Abner Lowry, Jr. Obituary''']
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: 10 Nov 1873, '''Arlisha Jane Funk,''' in the L.D.S. Endowment House, ceremony performed by Daniel H.Wells.  Arlisha Jane Funk was born, 27 Sept 1857, in Manti, Sanpete, Utah to Daniel Buckley Funk and Mary Jane Pectol. 
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Louisa Jane Lowry,''' born, 4 Oct 1874, in Sterling, Sanpete, Utah. She was married by Abner Lowry to James P. Edwards, 15 May 1895.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sylvania Lowry''' was born, 9 May 1876, in Sterling, Sanpete, Utah. She was married to Peter Swensen, 28 Nov 1894. Manti Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Minnie Levern Lowry,''' was born, 19 May 1878, in Sterling, Utah. She was married to Charles W. Larsen, 22 July 1896,in Sterling by Abner Lowry.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Ada Arlisha Lowry,''' was born, 24 Aug 1880, in Manti. She was married lo Edwin Perry Works, 25 Jan 1905. Manti Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Abner D. Lowry''' was born, 12 July 1882, in Sterling. He married Annie Susan Cloward, 22 Jan 190^ in Manti Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Jesse William Lowry''' was born, 8 Aug 1884, in Sterling. He married Eliza Stutsnegger, 26 Sep 1906 in Manti sld,5 Dec 1906, in Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Blanch Lowry''' was born, 22 June 1886, in Manti. She married Jesse Christian Works, 2 May 1906,in Manti Temple.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''John Lowry,''''was born, 31 Apr 1888, in Sterling. He died, 12 Aug 1888 and was buried in Sterling. 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Mary Ellen Lowry''' was born, 14 Jan 1890, in Sterling. She died, 28 Jan 1890,and was buried in Sterling. Ida May Lowry was born, 2 May 1892, in Sterling. She was married to Charles P. Draper, 6 Sep 1911 in Manti Temple. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Abner Lowry Jr.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The son of Abner Lowry Sr., and Louisa Bradley. Born 14, April 1855. He was a large man of stature, he was a man of character. He was well versed in law, and political ventures. He served four years as Mayor of Moroni, Sanpete Co.
2 CONC  Utah. He was a single man when he was appointed to the position of Mayor, which he filled very well. He was a man who liked everything done when it should be done, and done well. He always said, "What was worth doing at all, was 
2 CONC worth doing well. "In the winter of 1873, he met and married Arlisha Jane Funk. The daughter of Daniel Buckley Funk, and Mary Jane Pectal. They loved in Moroni until the summer of 1874. They were married in the Endowment House in 
2 CONC Salt Lake City. They lived in Manti until the spring of 1875, when they moved to Sterling Utah, six miles south of Manti. At this time he went to farming. He would plant and irrigate the hills and hollows into all kinds of grasses
2 CONC , and red clover. He would raise hay to feed a large dairy herd. Abner was good sawmill man. He owned three mills which he opperate at different times. The Mill sites were located upon the Black Mountain. At the last site, the old
2 CONC  boiler still stands. Black Mountain is on the North end of 12-mile Canyon, closer to Mayfield than Sterling. They used the slabs for fuel to generate the steam that gave them power to saw the lumber with. They hauled the lumber b
2 CONC y oxen and horses to the valley and sold it for their lively-hood. At one time he owned and farmed land around Palisade Park. Also at one time he owned and operated a Meat Market/Boarding House in Marysvale. It burned down and lef
2 CONC t them with nothing but what they stood in. Abner and his family moved back to Manti and ran a Bakery, and Meat Market. All was going well with them until one day a fresh flood came down the creek and washed away all they had. (I 
2 CONC understand the flood was caused from over-grazing in the mountains to the east). The water master drowned at the time while trying to clear debris from the creek bed; it was in June of 1900, The watermasters name was Nils Rasmusse
2 CONC n. This was another hard blow. But true pioneers that they were, they never gave up. They moved back to Sterling and built a good home on a hill, which overlooks the town of Sterling. The house was made of adobes and it still stan
2 CONC ds today, 2003. It stands in memory of the sturdy, "never say die" people who erected it. and Arlisha always had other of their family living with them, but they never com neies Arlish always set a very good table, she as a good c
2 CONC ook. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000014661210096&photo_id=6000000207589155837&position=0 Abner Lowry, Jr Obituary]
2 CONT
