1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.rootsweb.ancestry.com/~utsanpet/Histories/TXTfiles/GEORGEPEAOCK.txt
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: Jul. 30, 1822, Farndale East, North, Yorkshire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Sep. 29, 1878, Manti, Sanpete County, Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT GEORGE DANIEL PEACOCK, son of George Peacock and Mary Noddings, was born in England July 30, 1822. The family removed to Canada, where his father died in 1831. His mother married John Clark, and in 1837, the family removed to the 
2 CONC United States, locating in Missouri.
2 CONT
2 CONT The next year they went to Iowa, where George, afterward known as "Judge Peacock," married Sarah Lowry April l4, 1840.
2 CONT
2 CONT In July of that year he was baptized in the Mormon Church and went to Nauvoo, Illinois, where he volunteered as a guard to the prophet Joseph Smith. In 1846 he left with the Saints and assisted in building the first ferry boat to 
2 CONC cross the Missouri River at Council Bluffs.  He came to Utah in 1850 and located at Manti.
2 CONT
2 CONT He served as Probate Judge and a member of the Territorial Legislature. He was the first postmaster in Manti. He performed a mission to England and was adjudant of the Sanpete military district during the Black Hawk war. He had th
2 CONC ree wives: Sarah, Mary and Sarah Belle, and left twenty-nine children. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Parents:
2 CONT
2 CONT George Peacock  
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Noddings Peacock Clark (1797 - 1858)
2 CONT
