1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: Mar. 8, 1857, Manti, Sanpete County, Utah, 
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: Oct. 15, 1909, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Manti Cemetery, Manti, Sanpete County Utah, USA, Plot: Lot 12 Blk 14 Plat B
2 CONT
2 CONT DEATH NOTICE: 
2 CONT
2 CONT The Manti Messenger, Thursday 21 October 1909:
2 CONT
2 CONT PEACOCK – In San Bernardino, Oct. 15, 1909. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Geo. Peacock, aged 52 years, 7 months and 7 days.
2 CONT
2 CONT DIES IN CALIFORNIA
2 CONT
2 CONT George Peacock, proprietor of the D & R G eating house in this city died in San Bernardino, California, last Friday.  About a month ago he and Mrs. Peacock went to Long Beach, California in hopes of improving his health.  He grew 
2 CONC worse, however and a change to San Bernardino was made but he lived there but a few days.  Mrs. Peacock returned Monday with the remains, relatives having met her at Salt Lake.
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Peacock was 52 years of age, well and favorably known and has quite a large number of relatives in this city but no children. The funeral was held Tuesday afternoon.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of George Daniel Peacock & Mary Artimesia Lowry Peacock, 1834-1910.  Husband of Lucy Smith Reid Tennant 1864 - 1929
2 CONT
2 CONT Created by: Vauna Mri Record added: Mar 10, 2009 Find A Grave Memorial# 34661702
2 CONT * '''Residence''': Manti, Sanpete, Utah, United States - 1860
2 CONT *
