1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Birth: Dec. 27, 1858, Manti, Sanpete County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Death: 	Oct. 1, 1920, Emery, Emery County Utah, USA
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Emery Cemetery, Emery, Emery County Utah, USA, Plot: F-19-06
2 CONT
2 CONT PEACOCK, BRIGHAM JAMES (son of George Peacock and Mary Artimesia Lowry), Born December 27, 1858, at Manti, Utah.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married Sarah Eleanor Cox Dec. 1, 1880, St. George, Utah (daughter of Frederick Walter Cox and Jemima Losee of Iowa).  She was born Nov. 30, 1859.  
2 CONT
2 CONT Their children: 
2 CONT
2 CONT Brigham James b. April 8, 1882, m. Lydia Pauline Sinker; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mima May b. Dec. 20, 1883, m. James Keele; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edgar Reid b. Nov. 20, 1885, d. infant; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Hazel Elvira b. March 16, 1887, m. William Keele; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Edward Lynn b. July 17, 1889, m. Mary Johannah Allred; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ralph Vernon b. June 5, 1891, m. Rosetta Jorgensen; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Byron Charles b. March 10, 1893; Eleanor b. July 23, 1896; 
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilbur b. June 29, 1899; Riddell b. April 30, 1903. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The family home was in Emery, Utah.  He was an Elder.  He settled at Emery 1895; moved to Sterling 1880, and engaged in the sheep business under firm name of B. J. Peacock & Sons.  Merchant and farmer.
2 CONT
