1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Susan Angeline was my great grandmother who lived most of her life  in Pettyville aka:Sterling Utah  which was the little town south of Manti, where she was born. Because I lived in Manti Utah for 11 years I was ab
2 CONC le to visit most of the places where this family lived most of their lives. All of Susan and Walter's children were born in Manti and Sterling. They lived on a farm at the edge of Sterling about 1/4 mile from town and the land con
2 CONC tinued rough and un-populated from there out into the lowlands and hills. There were no houses close by. The farm consisted of about 2 or 3 hundred acres with about 3 thousand head of sheep. The wool from the sheep was about the o
2 CONC nly source of income the family had. Years later Walter & Susan sold their farm and bought a general merchandise store in Sterling. The living quarters for their large family was in the back and the store was in the front. It was 
2 CONC a Grocery Store, Post office, Ice House, and a community Center. While Walter tended to the business, Susan kept the family organized. Everything always seemed to be well-organized and under complete control as told by my grandmot
2 CONC her, Mary Adeline Barton, 7th child in the family. The family lived in this house for about 8 years and the store in front furnished a good livelihood for the family until times got hard and many people began to ask for credit. Wa
2 CONC lter was so kinghearted because he knew they all had large families to feed that he never refused credit to any of his neighbors. Consequently he went broke and had to sell out. Next the family moved up to Morrison about 3 miles e
2 CONC ast of Sterling in Sterling Canyon. Walter and two of his sons went to work in the coal mine while Susan ran a boarding house for the mine workers. She had 15 to 20 boarders most of the time and the girls in the family had to work
2 CONC  with their Mother. Walter also went in on a business venture and established and maintained a boarding house  at the rock quarry up in the Nephi Canyon. Susan worked hard at the Boarding house for 10 years and then they moved to 
2 CONC Manti in about 1905 where Walter bought a Livery stable and ran that for several years. Walter ran the "hack" that met the trains and brought passengers to town and Susan kept a few boarders and some roomers didnt have anywhere el
2 CONC se to stay. Susan died in 1927 in Ogden Utah and was buried in the Manti Cemetery. Written by Susan L Beus 
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.myheritage.com/research/record-1-246353621-1-501658/susan-angeline-barton-born-petty-in-myheritage-family-trees MyHeritage Family Trees] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jul 
