2 CONT Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bartlett and her family were described in pages 21 - 22 of the published source, The Descendants of Joseph Bartlett:
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bartlett, born Newton, Mass., July 26, 1697; died Dec. 7, 1774, in his 78th year; married March 12, 1719, Mary Bartlett. She was born May 6, 1701; died Jan. 15, 1751. She was daughter of Benjamin and Mary Bartlett, and her 
2 CONC birth is said to be the first birth recorded in the Brookfield records. Her father was probably the Benjamin Bartlett, who with his brother, Jehoida, was a new comer to Brookfield, in 1700; they were the sons of Benjamin and Debor
2 CONC ah (Barnard) Bartlett, of Windsor, Conn., and grandsons of John Bartlett, who was a resident of Windsor in 1649.[1]
2 CONT Birth
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bartlett (Bartlit, Bartlet), daughter of Benjamin Bartlett and Mary Clesson, was born on May 6, 1701 in Brookfield, Worcester, Province of Massachusetts Bay[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Marriage
2 CONT
2 CONT Thomas Bartlett (Bartlit, Bartlet) and Mary Bartlett (Bartlit, Bartlet), were married on March 12, 1719 in Brookfield, Worcester, Province of Massachusetts Bay. [3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Death
2 CONT
2 CONT Mary Bartlit (Bartlett), wife of Thomas, died on January 15, 1751 in Brookfield, Worcester, Province of Massachusetts Bay.
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
