2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bull was born January 5, 1677 in Donnington, Gloucestershire, England. He was the son of Isaac Bull and Mary Unknown.
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Closson, 4th child of Josiah Closson and Mary Williamson in 1707, in Rhode Island.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bull was called a miller in North Kingston, Rhode Island. He and Mary had ten children, of whom one, Ruth, may have died young as no further record of her has been found. They were:
2 CONT
2 CONT Isaac, b. 22 July 1708 Jamestown, Rhode Island. He married Rebecca Browning
2 CONT John 08 June 1710 S. Kingston, Rhode Island married Lydia Closson
2 CONT Hannah, b. 1712 m. Eben Harrington
2 CONT Josiah, b.1714 S. Kingston, Rhode Island, married Ruth Tripp
2 CONT Nathan, b.1715 S. Kingston, Rhode Island, married Abigail Inman (n?)
2 CONT Ruth, b.1717 S. Kingston, Rhode Island
2 CONT Timothy, b. 1720 S. Kingston, Rhode Island, married Patience Page
2 CONT Jeremiah, b. 1722 S. Kingston, Rhode Island married, (1) Abigail Man(n), married (2) Ruth Closson
2 CONT Jacob, b.1725 S. Kingston, Rhode Island, married Rebecca Gamage
2 CONT Abigail, b. 1727, married Abraham Palmer
2 CONT
2 CONT Six of their sons, (all except John), moved into New York Colony about the same time, some settling in Dutchess County. Some went to Vermont, the southern part of which was New York at that time. During, and following, the Revolut
2 CONC ionary War, some of their descendants went into Quebec and some eventually migrated across Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT He died in 1724 in Rhode Island, [1]
2 CONT
2 CONT All the Bull families who descended from Isaac Bull were Quakers, at least for one or two more generations.
2 CONT
2 CONT John Bull (1677 - 1724)
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===John Bull===
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Born 5 Jan 1677 in Donnington, Gloucestershire, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Isaac Bull and Mary (Unknown) Bull
2 CONT
2 CONT Brother of Elizabeth (Bull) Vaughan, Mary (Bull) Mowry, Rose Bull and Hannah (Bull) Phillips [half]
2 CONT
2 CONT Husband of Mary (Closson) Bull — married 1707 in So Kingston, W, Washington, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Father of Isaac Bull Sr, Josiah Bull Sr., Nathan Bull, Timothy Bull and Abigail (Bull) Palmer
2 CONT
2 CONT Died 1724 at about age 46 in Kingstown, Providence, Rhode Island
2 CONT
2 CONT Profile last modified 12 Mar 2023 | Created 19 Sep 2010
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources
2 CONT
2 CONT ↑ https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/71080034
2 CONT * Dutchess County, NY: The Settlers of the Beekman Patent, Vol. 2, pp. 845-847, New England Historic Genealogical Society (Online Database).
2 CONT
2 CONT Wilbour, Benjamin Franklin, comp., Little Compton Families, Volume 1, Baltimore, Maryland: Reprinted for Clearfield Co. by Genealogical Publishing Co. (2003), 192.
2 CONT The Genealogical Dictionary of Rhode Island: Comprising Three Generations of Settlers who came before 1690. John Osbourne Austin. Clearfield, Albany, NY. 1887
2 CONT Young, Mary Lynch. Descendants of Josiah Bull, Jr. (1738-1813) of Dutchess County, N.Y. and His Ancestry. Pg. 4.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT http://wintersmithbooks.com/genealogy/bull
2 CONT
2 CONT JOHN JONATHAN BULL was born in 1677in England. He married Mary Closson daughter of Josiah Closson and Mary Williamson in 1707, in Rhode Island.  On 15 JUL 1707, he desired liberty to live in town, if he could get a house. His requ
2 CONC est was granted, if he be no way troublesome to the town. Children: (births of Isaac and John recorded at Jamestown Rhode Island). John died in Providence, R.I.
2 CONT
2 CONT CHILDREN of John BULL and Mary CLOSSON
2 CONT
2 CONT     Isaac Bull, born 22 JUL 1708. He was of Jamestown, Rhode Island. He married on 8 APR 1731 Rebecca BROWNING.
2 CONT
2 CONT     John Bull. Born on 8 June 1710 in South Kingston, Rhode Island. He married Lydia CLOSSON.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Hannah Bull. Born in 1712. She married Eben HARRINGTON.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Josiah Bull. Born in 1713-1714 in North Kingston, Rhode Island. He married Ruth TRIPP in 1737. He died in 1813 in Beekman Precinct, Duchess County, New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Nathan Bull. Born in 1715 in South Kingston, Rhode Island. He married Abigail INMAN in 1739. He died in 1791 in Rutland, Vermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Ruth Bull. Born in 1717.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Timothy Bull. Born in 1720 in South Kingston, Rhode Island. He married Patience PAGE. He died in 1810 in Vermont.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jeremiah Bull. Born in 1722 in South Kingston, Rhode Island. He married Abigail MANN.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Jacob Bull. Born in 1725. He married Rebecca GAMAGE.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Abigail Bull. Born in 1727. She married Abraham PALMER.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
