1 NOTE {geni:about_me} The descendants of William and Elizabeth Tuttle, who came from old to New England in 1635, and settled in New Haven in 1639, with numerous biographical notes and sketches : also, some account of the descendants of 
2 CONC John Tuttle, of Ipswich; and Henry Tuthill, of Hingham, Mass. (1883)
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.archive.org/stream/descendantsofwil01tutt#page/n821/mode/2up
2 CONT
2 CONT William Tuttle & Elizabeth
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. Sarah Tuttle, bap. April 1642; m. in New Haven Nov. 19, 1663, John Slauson (Slason-Slosson), s. of Geo. Slauson of Stamford. In 1700 John Slauson and Joseph Ferris were appointed constable in S. The same year he was rated (engl
2 CONC ish pound)101. Mrs. Sarah Slauson d. Nov. 17, 1676. He m. (2) Elizabeth Benedict (dau. of Thomas of Norwalk, who was delegate to Assembly 1664; Lieut. 1665; town clerk 1666; selectman, deputy May, 1670-75, and deacon many years). 
2 CONC  By 2d wife John Slauson had Mary, b. April 21, 1680; Thomas, March 12, 1781; Hannah, b. March 12, 1685. He d. Oct. 16, 1706; Inv. Nov. 29, 1706, (english pound)285. Est. settled jan. 11, 1706-7 by John, Jonathan, Thomas, Sarah, w
2 CONC ife of Ebenezer Bishop, Elizabeth, wife of Nathaniel Pond, and Mary Slason. (App.)
2 CONT
2 CONT I. John Slauson, b. Sept. 9, 1664; "a bright boy" in 1671; m. MARY __.
2 CONT
2 CONT II. Sarah Slauson, Jan. 20, 1667; m. Oct. 2, 1700, Ebenezer Bishop.
2 CONT
2 CONT III. Jonathan Slauson, July 25, 1670; m. Feb. 4, 1699, Mary Waterbury.
2 CONT
2 CONT IV. Elizabeth Slauson, Jan. 30, 1672; m. Nathaniel Pond.
2 CONT
2 CONT -----------------------
