1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GRid=39815210 '''Margery ''Smith'' Platt'''] Find A Grave Memorial# 39815210
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Margery Smith is the daughter of John and Martha Smith. She married Timothy Platt 22 Aug 1728 Redding, Fairfield, Ct. Children are Abigail, Timothy, Hezekiah, Jesse, Anne, Jesse, Zebulon.
2 CONT
2 CONT In the book of Marriages and Births at the Clerks Office at Fairfield page 143
2 CONT "Timothy Platt son of Jonas Platt and Margery Smith daughter of John Smith were married Aug 22 1728"
2 CONT
2 CONT Timothy's Will
2 CONT
2 CONT On 13 May 1736, he was mentioned as "my youngest" brother in the will of Zebulon Platt of Huntington.
2 CONT On 10 May 1741, he was admitted to the church at Redding on the recommendation of Rev. Mr. Chapman.
2 CONT The will of Timothy Platt was dated 22 September 1784, proved 2 January 1787. Inventory was taken 2 January 1787 and recorded 4 December 1787. The will reads:
2 CONT "In the Name of God Amen.
2 CONT I Timothy Platt of Redding in Fairfield County and State of Connecticut in New England being in a weak state as to bodily health but of sound disposing mind and memory; calling to mind my own mortality and knowing that it is appoi
2 CONC nted to all once to die; to make and ordaine this my last will and Testament and first of all I give my soul into the hand of God who gave it cheerfully trusting in his covenanted mercy in Jesus Christ for the salvation thereof an
2 CONC d my body I recommend to the Earth to be decently buried at the Discretion of my Executors hereinafter named nothing doubting of the Glorious Resurrection and hoping for eternal Life (through Jesus Christ our Lord) and as touching
2 CONC  that worldly estate with which it hath pleased God to bless me, I give bequeath and devise in manner following.
2 CONT Imprimis. My will is that all my just debts and funeral charges shall be first paid and satisfied.
2 CONT Item. Whereas my beloved wife Rebeckah and I entered into marriage / made a covenant by way of jointer, my is that said covenant of jointer be truly and faithfully fulfilled.
2 CONT Item. I will and bequeath to my beloved son Timothy Platt the sum of ten pounds lawfull money (to be his forever) which I suppose will (together with what he had already had) be his proportionable part of my estate besides paying 
2 CONC him for the time he served me after he was twenty one years of age.
2 CONT Item. I will and bequeath to my beloved son Hezekiah Platt over and above what he has already had of my Estate the sum of five shillings lawfull money to be his forever.
2 CONT Item. I will and bequeath to two of my sons viz Jesse Platt and Zebulon Platt ninety one pounds thirteen shillings each in consideration of their not receiving their proportionable part of my estate so soon after their arriving to
2 CONC  the age of twenty one years as my others sons did.
2 CONT Item. I will and bequeath to [ ^ my] son Zebulon Platt the west end of my dwelling house to be his forever. moreover it is my will that a certain piece of land lying in a place called the Great Meadows which I [deeded to three of 
2 CONC my sons viz: Hezekiah, Jesse & Zebulon shall be considered as a part of their portion of my Estate and shall be counted to them at thirty shillings per acre.
2 CONT Furthermore it is my Will that what I have charged upon my Book of accounts against any of my children shall be reckoned as so much toward their portion as they stand respectively charged.
2 CONT Item. I will and bequeath to three of my sons viz. Hezekiah Jesse and Zebulon Platt and my two Daughters viz. Abigail the wife of Nathaniel Hull and Anne the wife of Hezekiah Whitelock all the remaining part of my estate if any th
2 CONC ere should be to be theirs forever but to be divided amongst them in the following proportion viz each of my said sons viz Hezekiah Jesse & Zebulon shall have fifty shillings to each of my said Daughters viz Abigail & Annes twenty
2 CONC  shillings and each of my said daughters shall have twenty shillings to [ ^ each] said sons fifty shillings and in this already willed away.
2 CONT Item. I do hereby constitute and appoint two of [ ^ my] sons viz Jesse and Zebulon Platt to be the joint Executors of this my last Will & Testament.
2 CONT Finally I do hereby revoke all former Wills Testaments or Executors by me made or appointed ratifying this and no other to be my last will and testament in witness whereof I have hereunto set my Hand & Seal this twenty second day 
2 CONC of September AD 1784. N.B. the words my each my were inserted before signing and sealing
2 CONT Signed sealed published and
2 CONT declared by Timothy Platt
2 CONT to be his last Will and Testament
2 CONT in presence of Timothy Platt
2 CONT Joseph Banks
2 CONT Daniel Lyon
2 CONT Jesse Banks"
2 CONT Distribution was made 2 December 1789:
2 CONT "1st Distributed and set off to Widow Rebecca Platt, as her Dower, for her to use, improve, and peaceably enjoy so long as she shall remain the widow of the sd Deceased viz: the east end of the dwelling house ... ground for a gard
2 CONC en ... one acre of the old orchard ... plowland ...
2 CONT 2d Distributed and set off to Timothy Platt ... six acres ...
2 CONT 3rd Distributed to Hezk Platt part of a Note against himself for the sum of five shillings
2 CONT 4th Distributed and set off to Jesse Platt ... [several parcels of land] ...
2 CONT 5th Distributed to Zebulon Platt ... [several parcels of land] ..."
2 CONT 9
