1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT === Eliphalet Lockwood
2 CONT * Birth: 27 Feb 1675, Norwalk, Fairfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * Death; 14 Oct 1753 (aged 78), Norwalk, Fairfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT * Burial: Town House Hill Cemetery, Norwalk, Fairfield County, Connecticut, USA
2 CONT *Parents: Ephraim Lockwood and Mercy St. John
2 CONT * Spouse: Mary Gould - married 11 October 1699.  Daughter of John Gold of Stamford.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Representative from Norwalk to General Assembly in May, 1724.
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Biography
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Lockwood-1272
2 CONT
2 CONT Eliphalet Lockwood, son of Ephraim, was born 27 Feb. 1675/6 in Norwalk, Fairfield County, Connecticut.[1][2]
2 CONT
2 CONT He married Mary Gold, daughter of John Gold of Stamford, on 11 Oct. 1699.[2]
2 CONT
2 CONT Eliphalet died 14 Oct. 1753 at Norwalk, Farifield County, Connecticut and was buried there[2] at Town House Hill Cemetery, Norwalk, Connecticut. His memorial has photos of his headstone with the inscription:"Here lies the body of 
2 CONC Mr. Eliphalet Lockwood who departed this life in the 78th year of his age, October ye 14th 1753" and links to those of family members.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT Alternative birth/death: Feb. 27, 1675 and Oct. 14, 1763.[4]
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will dated 1753 mentions his children, Eliphalet, Peter, Damaris, Mary, and Abigail. His wife, Mary, is to be his sole Executrix.[2] His inventory was taken on 11 December 1753. He continues the enslavement of his black man
2 CONC  Mingo by bequeathing him to his wife.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Children of Eliphalet and Mary
2 CONT # Hannah b. 28 July 1700. d. 1712.[2]
2 CONT # Damaris b. 7 Nov. 1701 m. John Betts, Jr.[2]
2 CONT # a son b. 28 Nov. 1703. d. 20 Dec. 1703.[2]
2 CONT # Mary b. 4 Nov. 1704.[2].  ''Married Martin Kellogg.''
2 CONT # Eliphalet b. 24 June 1706.[2]
2 CONT # John b. 8 Jan. 1707/8 d. 17 Oct. 1734.[2]
2 CONT # Mercy b. 11 April 1709, d. 1 Oct. 1712.[2]
2 CONT # Peter b. 16 Mar. 1710/1 m. twice.[2]
2 CONT # Hannah b. 12 July 1712, d. 27 Oct. 1713.[2]
2 CONT # Abigail b. 17 Oct. 1716. [2]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family notes
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gold-625
2 CONT
2 CONT >Her [Mary Lockwood's] will is dated 23 March 1759 and witnesses were sworn on 10 April 1761 In Norwalk and proved on 6 April 1762 in Fairfield. She mentions her daughter Damaras Betts, wife of John Betts, her grandson, Eliphalet 
2 CONC Kellogg, and her son Peter Lockwood.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Kelloggs in the Old world and the New," by Hopkins, Timothy, 1859-1937 (Publication date 1903). Page 82.  < [https://archive.org/details/kelloggsinoldwor01hopk/page/82/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 207. Martin,5 son of Samuel4 (47), b. in Norwalk, 23 Mar., 1711; m. Mary Lockwood, dau. of Deacon Eliphalet Lockwood, b. 27 Feb., 1675-76, and Mary Gold, b. 1674, of Stamford.
2 CONT
2 CONT She d. ; he m. (2) Mercy (perhaps dau. of Samuel Wood, of Norwalk, who had a dau. Mercy, b. 30 Mar., 1717). He d. 7 July, 1756.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Inscription'''
2 CONT here lies the body of mr eliphalet lockwood who departed this life in the 78th year of his age, october 14th 1753.
2 CONT ----
