1 NAME Mary /Lockwood/
2 GIVN Mary
2 SURN Lockwood
2 _MARNM Kellogg
2 NICK Mercy "Kellogg"
2 NICK not Lockman
2 NICK not Hanford
1 SEX F
1 BIRT
2 DATE 4 NOV 1704
2 ADDR
3 CITY Norwalk
3 STAE Connecticut
1 DEAT
2 DATE BET 1753 AND 1756
2 ADDR
3 CITY New Canaan
3 STAE Connecticut
3 CTRY United States
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Not the same as https://www.geni.com/people/Mercy-Hanford/6000000210531604823?through=6000000003942570385
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT "The Kelloggs in the Old world and the New," by Hopkins, Timothy, 1859-1937 (Publication date 1903). Page 82.  < [https://archive.org/details/kelloggsinoldwor01hopk/page/82/mode/2up Archive.Org] >
2 CONT
2 CONT 207. Martin,5 son of Samuel4 (47), b. in Norwalk, 23 Mar., 1711; m. Mary Lockwood, dau. of Deacon Eliphalet Lockwood, b. 27 Feb., 1675-76, and Mary Gold, b. 1674, of Stamford.
2 CONT
2 CONT She d. ; he m. (2) Mercy (perhaps dau. of Samuel Wood, of Norwalk, who had a dau. Mercy, b. 30 Mar., 1717). He d. 7 July, 1756.
2 CONT
2 CONT He and his wife joined the church in New Canaan Parish, 2 Feb., 1743. His will, dated 3 July, 1756, proved 30 July, same year, mentions his wife, Mercy, dau. Mercy, sons Eliphalet, Martin, Samuel and Nathan. His brother-in-law, Th
2 CONC eophilus Fitch, and his brother, Epenetus Kellogg (211), were the executors. Besides one-quarter of his real estate, he gives to "Eliphalet in consideration of his being my eldest son and other considerations the following article
2 CONC s which were '''his own mother's''' * * also two cows and a calf, — the cows are those which his grandmother Lockwood gave to me."
2 CONT
2 CONT She m. (2) 22 Mar., 1757, Capt. Samuel Hanford, of New Canaan; d. 28 Dec, 1783, aged 66.
2 CONT
2 CONT Children.
2 CONT
2 CONT # +581 Eliphalet, b. before 1740; m. Sarah Brown.
2 CONT # +582 Martin, b. 10 Oct., 1740; m. (1) Mercy Benedict; (2) Abigail Knapp.
2 CONT # 583 Samuel,bap. 16 Oct., 1743; d. young.
2 CONT # +584 Mercy, bap. 1 Sept., 1745 ; m. Moses Hanford.
2 CONT # +585 Samuel, b. 29 June, 1749; m. (1) Elizabeth Waring; (2) Mrs. Lydia (Smith) Crane.
2 CONT # 586 Nathan bap. 26 Apr., 1752; m. Rachel Carter.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
