2 CONT >In his will dated 1753 [Eliphalet Lockwood] mentions his children, Eliphalet, Peter, Damaris, Mary, and Abigail. His wife, Mary, is to be his sole Executrix.[2] His inventory was taken on 11 December 1753. He continues the enslav
2 CONC ement of his black man Mingo by bequeathing him to his wife.[5]
2 CONT
2 CONT https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Gold-625
2 CONT
2 CONT >Her [Mary Lockwood] will is dated 23 March 1759 and witnesses were sworn on 10 April 1761 In Norwalk and proved on 6 April 1762 in Fairfield. She mentions her daughter Damaras Betts, wife of John Betts, her grandson, Eliphalet Ke
2 CONC llogg, and her son Peter Lockwood.[1]
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
