2 CONT From the Green Bay Press-Gazette, Tuesday, April 26, 1932
2 CONT GEORGE W. MOTT DIES HERE MONDAY NIGHT
2 CONT George W. Mott, 84, died Monday evening at 8:15 o"clock at the home of his daughter, Mrs Michael Lausten, 318 S. Quincy St., death being due to infirmities of advanced age. He was born in Canada and lived in Shawano County for app
2 CONC roximately 60 years, before coming to Green Bay to live with his daughter seven years ago.
2 CONT Besides Mrs Lausten, Mr Mott leaves six children, Mrs John Liesch, Roselawn, Joseph, Gladstone, Mich., Eldon, Chattanooga, Okla., George Jr., Seymour, Perry, Wabeno, and Walter, Green Bay. The body will be at the Lausten home unti
2 CONC l Thursday when it will be removed to the Muehl funeral home at Seymour where services will be held at 2 p.m.  Burial will be at Seymour.
