1 NOTE {geni:about_me} === GEDCOM Note ===
2 CONT from the Marinette (WI)  Daily News, Saturday, March 11, 1905, p. 7
2 CONT DEATH OF MRS. WOOD
2 CONT Wife of J.J. Wood Dies At Menominee Hospital Friday Evening
2 CONT Mrs. Lucy A. Wood, wife of John J. Wood, died at the St, Joseph's Hosiptal (sic) at Menominee, Mich., Friday evening the 10th inst.  Mrs. Wood was taken from her home here to the hospital three weeks ago last Tuesday, where she un
2 CONC derwent an operation for appendicitis, from which she seemed to be recovering, until complications of kidney trouble set in, and from which her death was caused.
2 CONT Mrs. Wood was born Oct. 8, 1851, in Lynn, Ontario, and when a young girl came to Gibson, Wis., with her parents.  She was married to Mr. Wood in 1869 and in the fall of 1872, Mr. and Mrs. Wood came to Peshtigo, where they have sin
2 CONC ce resided.  Beside (sic) her husband, she leaves seven children, viz., Mrs. Mary A. Jones, Atlantic, Iowa; Mrs. Etta Nelson, Mrs. Alma Parish, and Mrs. Bert Constine; Otto, Howard, and Lawrence Wood, all of Peshtigo.  Her mother,
2 CONC  Mrs. Rebecca Mott, and two brothers, and four sisters, also survive her.  One of the brothers still resides in Canada, and the other brother, sisters, and mother are residents of Atlantic, Iowa.  Mrs. Wood was a kind and loving w
2 CONC ife and mother and the vacancy which her death has caused in the home can never be filled.  The family have the sympathies of the entire community in their sad hour of bereavement.
2 CONT The funeral will be held: Sunday afternoon in the Peshtigo Congregational church, at 2:30, the Rev. Soule officiating.
