2 CONT from the Atlantic (IA) News Telegraph, Monday, May 20, 1946
2 CONT Mrs. Mary Ann Pellett, 92, wife of the late George J. Pellett, died at 1:15 yesterday morning at the Atlantic Hospital as the result of a hip fracture which she suffered last Tuesday afternoon.  She had been at the hospital four d
2 CONC ays.
2 CONT She was born in Brockville, Canada, Feb 9, 1854, the daughter of Richard and Rebecca Brown Mott, and came to the United States with her parents when she was a girl.  She was married at Manitowoc, Wis., to Mr. Pellett Feb. 23, 1876
2 CONC , and they moved to a farm north of Atlantic that year.  In 1909, they moved to Atlantic, where Mr Pellett died Jan. 3, 1925.
2 CONT Mrs. Pellett affiliated with the Methodist Church when she was a girl and was active in the Buck Creek church while living north of here, and in the Atlantic Methodist church, in which she served as a Sunday school teacher for a n
2 CONC umber of years.  She was a charter member and later an honorary member of the Home Improvement club.
2 CONT Surviving are two daughters, Mrs. W. R. Jones and Mrs C. W. Savery of Atlantic; a son, W. G. Pellett, of Atlantic; two step daughters, Mrs. Mary Archer of Omaha and Mrs J. L. White of Manchester, IA.; a stepson, Walter J Pellett o
2 CONC f Council Bluffs; eight grand children and 11 great grandchildren.  A son, Bert T. Pellett died April 1, 1935, and a daughter, Miss Adah Pellett died last March 28.
2 CONT Funeral services will be held Tuesday at 2 pm at the Roland Peacock & Baxter funeral home, the Rev. L. D. Thomas officiating, assisted by the Rev. C. W. Hohanshelt.  Interment will be in the Atlantic Cemetery.  The remains will be
2 CONC  at the funeral home until the service hour.
