1 TITL Reverend
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT
2 CONT Descendant of Mayflower passengers John Howland and Elizabeth (Tilley) Howland
2 CONT ----
2 CONT Born June 13, 1787 in Newfane, married Huldah Chipman of Sherham, Vt., and they had four children- Silas, Seraph Huldah, Ephraim Holland Jr., and John Marshall -who were all born in Malboro, Vt. while their father was pastor of th
2 CONC e Congregational Church. He built a home there in 1814, in which they lived until 1833, when he became pastor of the Presbyterian Church in Glen Falls, NY. In 1836, he received a call from the Prebyterian Church in Cambridge, NY -
2 CONC known as the "Old White Meeting House". On retiring from the pastorate there, he was principal of the Cambridge Washington Academy for a number of years. He died in Cambridge in 1864.
