1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Samuel Hopkins, Vestryman 1848-1866; Warden 1866-1873; b. N. Y. City, Nov. 2, 1809; d. Catskill, N. Y., Jan. 9, 1882; s. Freeman and Phebe (Davis) Hopkins; m. Troy, N. Y., Susan Elizabeth Gardner. Was educated in N
2 CONC . Y. City and engaged in business as an iron merchant. He was connected with the Seaman's Mission and the Society for Improving the Condition of the Poor, and was a teacher in St. George's Sunday-school.
