1 NOTE {geni:about_me} U.S. Congressman. He was a successful iron merchant and a member of the New York State Assembly, (1885-86). In 1887, he was elected as a Republican to the Fiftieth Congress, serving until 1889. After his term, he w
2 CONC as watchman in the customhouse at New York City, in 1890. The circumstances of his death at age 43 were unclear when he was found dead by a train crew alongside the railroad tracks near Pleasantville, New Jersey.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bio by: John "J-Cat" Griffith
