1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Jeanie Thomas Lincoln (Gould)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/75728692/jeanie-thomas-lincoln Find A Grave Memorial ID # 75728692]
2 CONT
2 CONT Jeanie Gould Lincoln, author, was born in Troy, New York on May 28, 1853; daughter of Judge George and Sarah MaConn (Vail) Gould; granddaughter of Judge James and Sally McCurdy (Tracy) Gould and of George and Jane (Thomas) Vail. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Her father was Chief Justice of the Court of Appeals for the state of New York. She was educated under tutors and governesses and devoted herself to literary work. She was married, January 10, 1877 to Nathan Smith Lincoln, M.D., L
2 CONC L.D. 
2 CONT
2 CONT She was elected a member of the Society of American Authors in 1899. Her published volumes include: ''A Chaplet of Leaves'' (1869); ''Marjorie's Quest'' (1872); ''Her Washington Season'' (1884); ''A Genuine Girl'' (1896); ''An Unw
2 CONC illing Maid'' (1897) and ''A Pretty Tory'' (1899).
