1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Andrew Payne settled here in October, 1855, coming from New York. He was a brother-in-law of Alru Peck and came here with him. He had a family of ten children, named as follows: E.N. Payne, married and lives in Fay
2 CONC ette County; Helen was married to Charles Tulloch but soon after died; Hiram, married and lives in Fayette County; Frederick, married and lives in Byron Township; Mary W., is married and also lives in Byron; William is married and
2 CONC  lives in Byron; Julia, unmarried; Elizabeth, married to Sylvanus Taylor and resides in Washington Township; Sarah, is married to Sewell Butler, and lives in the State of Illinois; the youngest is Henry. Mr. Payne died in the town
2 CONC ship where the prime of his manhood was passed, in February 1874. His widow sold the property in Fremont and moved into Byron Township, where she still lives. He was a member of the Methodist Episcopal Church.
2 CONT
2 CONT History of Buchanan County - 1881.
2 CONT
2 CONT Andrew married Abigail Peck 15 August 1828 at Gilboa, Schoharie, N.Y. at the Reformed Dutch Church.
