2 ADDR
3 CITY Peekskill
3 STAE New York
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Mrs. Emma Hartshorn, wife of Matthew J. Lefevre, passed away at her home, No. 155 Fremont street, on Tuesday morning last. She had been ill more or less for a number of years, but was only confined to tho bed for t
2 CONC he past three weeks. The deceased was born in New York City and was in the 86th year of her age. She was the daughter of tho late Chas. E. and Mary J. Hartshoru. Thirty throe years ago sho was married to Mr. Lefevre, and they came
2 CONC  to Peeks-kill to live about twenty-five years ago. Mrs. Lefevre was a woman of kindly disposition aud her constant aim in life was to give others pleasure. That she accomplished that aim is attested by the large circle of friends
2 CONC  and acquaintances she made. Her charitable acts were numerous, although unostentatiously performed. The deceased is survived by her husband, and two sisters, Mrs. Anna L. Ingham and Mrs. Ida E. Peene, and three brothers, Charles 
2 CONC E. Hartshorn, Jr., David O. Hartshorn and Frank O. Hartshorn, all of Yonkers. The funeral services were held from her late residence yesterday (Friday) afternoon at oue o'clock, and were con-ducted by the Rev. C. A. Holla, assisto
2 CONC d by the Rev. J. E. Gors
2 CONT
2 CONT Highland Democrat
2 CONT February 4,1905
2 CONT
2 CONT * https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/69045831/emeline-h-lefevre
