1 NOTE {geni:about_me}   
2 CONT Israel was the son of John Miller and Julia A. Hoffman. He was born on 10 July 1839 near Fort Wayne, Indiana. Israel served three years in Civil War in the 152nd Indiana Infantry. His first wife was Harriet Beck, with whom he had 
2 CONC three children. At the time he was married to Harriet, Israel was a locomotive engineer on Wabash Railroad, running a passenger train between Fort Wayne and Toledo, OH. 
2 CONT Israel bought a flourmill at Fort Wayne with A.C. and D.S. Beaver, and on 24 July 1867, he married Susan Cornelia Totten. They had three children. Susan died in Fort Wayne on 22 November 1876. In the spring of 1878, the mill burne
2 CONC d. 
2 CONT Before the fall of 1878, Israel married Florence Palmer, and in the fall of 1878, the family moved to Grundy County, Tennessee, for the benefit of Israel’s health. They lived in Tennessee for six years, where three of Florence and
2 CONC  Israel’s four children were born. 
2 CONT In 1884, the family moved to Litchfield, MN. In Litchfield, Israel was the chief engineer in the construction of the Litchfield water works and electric light system. Florence and Israel’s fourth child was born in Litchfield in 18
2 CONC 91. 
2 CONT Sometime after 1891, Israel and Florence moved to Phoenix, AZ, with the younger children. In Phoenix, Israel operated the city water plant. 
2 CONT At some point, Israel moved to California, where he died on 16 July 1911 at Redondo Beach, CA. He was buried in Hollywood Cemetery in Los Angeles. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Harriet Beck:
2 CONT •	Frank M. Miller m. Clara Beaver
2 CONT •	Laura B. Miller m. Moore Milburn
2 CONT •	William H. Miller m. Mamie Koerner
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Susan Cornelia Totten:
2 CONT •	Susan L. Miller m. Chas. E. Phelps 
2 CONT •	Julia A. Miller 
2 CONT •	Jennie C. Miller m. William M. Meyers 
2 CONT
2 CONT Children with Florence Palmer:
2 CONT •	Mary E. Miller 
2 CONT •	John Miller (d. in infancy)
2 CONT •	Arthur G, Miller m. Florence Bradley 
2 CONT •	Clifford Miller m. Thelma Monroe
