1 NOTE {geni:about_me} He was a gentleman and liked to dress well.  I never had the pleasure of knowing him, he died before I was born.  Diane ......... He  is on the left in the photo of the three boys.
2 CONT
2 CONT He worked as the Head Concierge at the St. Regis Hotel in NYC. He had stories of rubbing elbows with the likes of W.C. Fields, Diamond Jim Brady and Mae West. He passed away when my dad was only 13, so the things I know are sparse
2 CONC . The thing that sticks out the most in my mind is that my father used to laugh at the last picture shown at the end of the opening to the show Cheers, and said that could double for his dad.  - Laura Kingery Alibrandi
