0 @N6000000000953524240@ NOTE
1 CONT Quotes from Joseph WORDEN---Dr. Stephen WORDEN was a Botanic Doctor.  He believed in going to mother earth for drugs.  I have seen many cases in my boyhood where Grandfather cured people that other noted doctors failed to do.  His
1 CONC  manner of treating patients was to sit a while and talk of ordenary things until they were rested and neves quited. Then he would place his hands or fingers on their wrist and study the circulation of the blood a few minutes, the
1 CONC n talk to them about their ailments.  The reply in every case would be Dr. you can tell my aches and pains beter then I can myself.  It was a mystery to me,  I's ask him how he could tell were the desise or pain was located his re
1 CONC ply - By knowing the circulation and normal condition of the blood. That long practice enabled him to detect any derangments in any part of the system.  For meny years he went far and near to relive pain ect.    One night in the d
1 CONC arkness his horse fell with him, and threw him on a rock and dislocated his sholder, broke his skull behind his ear.  He was found unconcious, bleeding from the ears and nose.  During the remainder of his life there was a depressi
1 CONC on on the skull on the right side of his head as large and as deep as the bowl of a teaspoon.
1 CONT
