0 @N6000000001169462553@ NOTE Name Prefix:<NPFX> Sir 
1 CONT John Claypoole was c. April 13, 1595, the son of Adam C laypoole
1 CONT and Dorothy Wingfield. He was knighted by Oliver Cromwell, a
1 CONT long ti me friend and associate. John Claypoole married Mary
1 CONT Angell in London on June 8, 1622. Mary was the daughter of
1 CONT William Angell Esq. and Joanne Povey. The An gell family traces
1 CONT to 1500 in Peakirk, Northamptonshire. Sir John Claypoole an d
1 CONT Mary had 14 children, of whom Norton was the 13th born in 1640.
1 CONT Their oldes t son John, born in 1623, married Elizabeth, daughter
1 CONT of Oliver Cromwell. Her tomb marker may still be seen at
1 CONT Westminster Abbey, the only Cromwell tomb not  removed at the
1 CONT time of the restoration. Sir John Claypoole died in 1664, and
1 CONT Mary Angell on April 10th, 1661. She was buried at Northborough,
1 CONT the ancestra l home of the Claypoole family, in the county of
1 CONT Northamptonshire.
1 CONT @S16@
0 @N6000000001169458863@ NOTE James Claypool was a friend of William Penn and went to the Americas to join him in Philadelphia.  Somewhere his line links up with Betsy Ross.
0 @N6000000001169461686@ NOTE OF Sussex County, Delaware 
1 CONT With Norton Claypoole we arrive at the first Americ an colonist
1 CONT in tracing the direct line of descent. Norton was c. on Oct. 16,
1 CONT 1640 in London, England to Sir John Claypoole and Mary Angell.
1 CONT He married Rach el about 1670 and arrived in America on the ship
1 CONT "Bachelor's Delight" via Barb ados on Feb. 22, 1678. His wife
1 CONT Rachel joined him coming from London in 1681. Norton had spent
1 CONT three years while in transit with his brother Edward in
1 CONT Barb ados. Norton and Rachel had six children: John in London in
1 CONT 1672 who died youn g; James 1673 in London; Mary 1682 in Lewes;
1 CONT Robert in 1683; Jeremiah in 1685;  and Elizabeth in 1687. James
1 CONT Claypoole, older brother of Norton, was a Quaker  and close
1 CONT associate of William Penn and arrived in the American colonies
1 CONT abo ut four years after Norton. A number of letters exist between
1 CONT the two brothers  in Delaware and London before James's arrival
1 CONT in Philadelphia. The descendent s of James Claypoole include
1 CONT Betsy Ross and Alfred Vanderbilt. The Plantagenet ancestry,
1 CONT largely unkown to the descendents of Norton Claypoole, was well
1 CONT kno wn to the descendents of James Claypoole in the 19th century.
1 CONT Norton Claypoole  owned 2000 acres in Delaware and was elected to
1 CONT the State Legislature in 1686 . Norton died at Lewes on May 15th,
1 CONT 1688. Rachel remarried Nehemiah Fields and  died Jan. 24, 1718.
1 CONT As no record of their marriage in 1670 is found, Rachel's  maiden
1 CONT name is not known. In researching this area, I have a theory
1 CONT that she  may have been a Rachel Joyce born in London to Robert
1 CONT and Rachel Joyce. To da te I have not found any conclusive proof
1 CONT of Rachel's maiden name. With this ge neration, we end the
1 CONT American portion of the direct line of descent and contin ue the
1 CONT remaining generations in England.
1 CONT @S8@S16@
1 CONT
1 CONT Norton left London for Barbados and then to Delaware with money loaned by brother James (the Quaker leader). This part of James' hope to establish additional sugar operations as brother David had done in Barbados. He left (in 1672
1 CONC ?), settling in now Sussex county Delaware. James housed Rachel until she finally left (perhaps on the ship Elizabeth & Mary), landed at Perth Amboy, with their son James, and was collected by Norton. They had another son Jeremiah
1 CONC  and daughter Elizabeth. After Norton died she married Nehemiah Field. James' letterbooks do not mention Rachel's family name.
1 CONT http://genforum.genealogy.com/cgi-bin/pageload.cgi?norton,rachel::claypool::629.html 
1 CONT ------------------------------------------
